    {
      "NamespaceHash": "36B95A4943D70F03C75FB3A5BDB8874B",
      "Source": "A list of all groups, and the variants within them, along with some misc data.<#RN#><#RN#>_________________________<#RN#>Tiers and their stat multipliers:<#RN#>1. Basic - 1x<#RN#>2. Delta - 2x<#RN#>3. Gamma - 4x<#RN#>4. Beta - 8x<#RN#>5. Alpha - 16x<#RN#>6. Elite - 32x<#RN#>7. Prime - 64x<#RN#>8. Apex - 128x<#RN#>9. Ultimate - 256x<#RN#>10. Ancient - 512x<#RN#>11. Endless - 1024x<#RN#>12. Omega - 2048x<#RN#>_________________________<#RN#><#RN#>How to Unlock each Tier:<#RN#><#RN#>-Basic through Elite spawn wild and can be tamed with appropriate kibble. You can upgrade your current tames to the next highest tier, up to Elite, by crafting a rank up token in the soul grinder using a Paragon soul of your tame's species.<#RN#>-Prime is unlocked by killing a Boss summoned from the beacon and feeding the soul to an Elite of the same variant.<#RN#>-Apex is unlocked by killing a Master summoned from the beacon and feeding the soul to a Prime of the same variant.<#RN#>",
      "Trans": {"SC":"A list of all groups, and the variants within them, along with some misc data.<#RN#><#RN#>_________________________<#RN#>Tiers and their stat multipliers:<#RN#>1. Basic - 1x<#RN#>2. Delta - 2x<#RN#>3. Gamma - 4x<#RN#>4. Beta - 8x<#RN#>5. Alpha - 16x<#RN#>6. Elite - 32x<#RN#>7. Prime - 64x<#RN#>8. Apex - 128x<#RN#>9. Ultimate - 256x<#RN#>10. Ancient - 512x<#RN#>11. Endless - 1024x<#RN#>12. Omega - 2048x<#RN#>_________________________<#RN#><#RN#>How to Unlock each Tier:<#RN#><#RN#>-Basic through Elite spawn wild and can be tamed with appropriate kibble. You can upgrade your current tames to the next highest tier, up to Elite, by crafting a rank up token in the soul grinder using a Paragon soul of your tame's species.<#RN#>-Prime is unlocked by killing a Boss summoned from the beacon and feeding the soul to an Elite of the same variant.<#RN#>-Apex is unlocked by killing a Master summoned from the beacon and feeding the soul to a Prime of the same variant.<#RN#>","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3722635761"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9C73C57041058CD01EBAC797DFB9937F",
      "Source": "Supernova",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Supernova","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3509870221"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0A34E7BD431122BE130A21AF6975CAAC",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Supernova</>: A massive AoE damage dealer. During combat, they can release a powerful Supernova blast that deals devistating damage to enemies and causes a very brief stun. Its best to avoid a Supernova creature until you're ready.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) causes a massive Supernova explosion, dealing significant damage to anything in the area along with a short stun.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Supernova Damage: 800% of Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Supernova Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Stun Length: 2s",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Supernova</>: A massive AoE damage dealer. During combat, they can release a powerful Supernova blast that deals devistating damage to enemies and causes a very brief stun. Its best to avoid a Supernova creature until you're ready.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) causes a massive Supernova explosion, dealing significant damage to anything in the area along with a short stun.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Supernova Damage: 800% of Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Supernova Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Stun Length: 2s","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2749737193"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "BE3AAB2B4582917E64352A896B4D52FB",
      "Source": "Meteor",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Meteor","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3370576343"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "06EC36A5446A60BE971F89897D2B3830",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Meteor</>: Meteor creatures can call down a small meteor strike in the area. While each individual meteor isn't particularly powerful, they hit over a large area, and larger enemies can be striken by multiple meteors leading to incredible health loss. The number of meteors can be random at times, as are the impact locations. Flying meteor dinos are able to quickly swoop over an area, barrage it with meteors and fly away, making them excellent for farming kills. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) calls down a cluster of meteors from the sky. They will impact random locations in the direct viscinity of the Meteor creature.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Number of Meteors: 12<#RN#>Meteor Target Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)<#RN#>Meteor Impact Damage: 300% of Ability Damage as Fire Damage<#RN#>Meteor Impact Radius: 900 (3 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Meteor</>: Meteor creatures can call down a small meteor strike in the area. While each individual meteor isn't particularly powerful, they hit over a large area, and larger enemies can be striken by multiple meteors leading to incredible health loss. The number of meteors can be random at times, as are the impact locations. Flying meteor dinos are able to quickly swoop over an area, barrage it with meteors and fly away, making them excellent for farming kills. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) calls down a cluster of meteors from the sky. They will impact random locations in the direct viscinity of the Meteor creature.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Number of Meteors: 12<#RN#>Meteor Target Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)<#RN#>Meteor Impact Damage: 300% of Ability Damage as Fire Damage<#RN#>Meteor Impact Radius: 900 (3 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1300024371"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "EECB8A1A4D78B1B6124D88937308DDBB",
      "Source": "Starfire",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Starfire","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2682529377"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B5D93CB64D3BE68E1691B1BE404953F7",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Starfire</>: Starfire creatures are able to create a small star that deals insane tick damage in an area. This star will set enemies on fire, and illuminate a massive area at night. Nightmare creatures are often afraid of this star, making them potentially lose their night time abilities or their willingness to attack. Starfire is one of the more powerful damage dealers over time. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a powerful star, which illuminates a huge area at night as well as dealing significant damage from the heat. <#N#><#N#>---<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Starfire Duration: 10 Seconds<#N#>Starfire Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Starfire Tick Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second As Fire Damage",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Starfire</>: Starfire creatures are able to create a small star that deals insane tick damage in an area. This star will set enemies on fire, and illuminate a massive area at night. Nightmare creatures are often afraid of this star, making them potentially lose their night time abilities or their willingness to attack. Starfire is one of the more powerful damage dealers over time. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a powerful star, which illuminates a huge area at night as well as dealing significant damage from the heat. <#N#><#N#>---<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Starfire Duration: 10 Seconds<#N#>Starfire Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Starfire Tick Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second As Fire Damage","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1707723513"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "27FEE47C4E66DD7FC46ACE9DE764ED9C",
      "Source": "Singularity",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Singularity","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3819116705"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "4BC37A0F41D66F5125657D8136F0B1DC",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Singularity</>: One of the worst things that can happen to you or your tames is being trapped in a Singularity. When a Singularity creature summons a black hole, it can rip enemies right up off of the ground, trapping them in the center while crushing them to death. A singularity will even pick up fish out of the ocean, killing them. Fortunately, its also makes for an absolutely devistating tame, as the singularity is not only able to deal great damage to enemies, but will trap them and prevent them from moving at the same time. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a singularity in front of you. This will have a very powerful gravity force, that will grab enemies off of the ground, sucking them in and crushing them until the singularity is gone.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30% <#N#>Singularity Initial Collapse Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Singularity Duration: 15 Seconds<#N#>Singularity Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Singularity Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second for 15 Seconds as Explosive Damage.<#N#>All Singularity Creatures are Immune to the Gravity Effect.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Singularity</>: One of the worst things that can happen to you or your tames is being trapped in a Singularity. When a Singularity creature summons a black hole, it can rip enemies right up off of the ground, trapping them in the center while crushing them to death. A singularity will even pick up fish out of the ocean, killing them. Fortunately, its also makes for an absolutely devistating tame, as the singularity is not only able to deal great damage to enemies, but will trap them and prevent them from moving at the same time. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a singularity in front of you. This will have a very powerful gravity force, that will grab enemies off of the ground, sucking them in and crushing them until the singularity is gone.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30% <#N#>Singularity Initial Collapse Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Singularity Duration: 15 Seconds<#N#>Singularity Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Singularity Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second for 15 Seconds as Explosive Damage.<#N#>All Singularity Creatures are Immune to the Gravity Effect.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3384424752"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "47C663A14049D4A61FD54BB63CAD8028",
      "Source": "Anti-Matter",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Anti-Matter","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3938361028"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "475BC3B545BC4CE8E68A54804791A1BA",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Anti-Matter</>: The 7th variant of Cosmic, Anti-Matter creatures' sole intended purpose is to modify ability cooldowns. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a blast that zeroeos out the cooldown on ally abilities, while triggering the cooldown timer on enemy abilities.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations).<#N#>Applies a buff to allies that prevents Anti-Matter cooldown reset for 5 seconds.<#N#>Applies a buff to enemies that prevents Anti-Matter cooldown trigger for 45 seconds.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Anti-Matter</>: The 7th variant of Cosmic, Anti-Matter creatures' sole intended purpose is to modify ability cooldowns. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a blast that zeroeos out the cooldown on ally abilities, while triggering the cooldown timer on enemy abilities.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations).<#N#>Applies a buff to allies that prevents Anti-Matter cooldown reset for 5 seconds.<#N#>Applies a buff to enemies that prevents Anti-Matter cooldown trigger for 45 seconds.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1649191988"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "3A7BCF4240FE19672304348D7672F926",
      "Source": "Gamma-Ray",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Gamma-Ray","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2263205925"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9F5AC9484EEBDCE1E78D328D02BC8AAD",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Gamma-Ray</>: Similar to Starfire in damage output, Gamma-Ray tears a hole in the sky to allow powerful gamma-rays to strike the ground, dealing reactive tick damage to enemies in the area. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) forces a Gamma-Ray to strike the ground in front of you, dealing tick damage to anything nearby until it goes away. The damage is dealt in a vertical cylinder in the location of the Gamma-Ray.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Gamma-Ray Duration: 10s<#N#>Gamma-Ray Radius: 1200 (4 Foundations)<#N#>Gamma-Ray Height: 6000 (20 Foundations)<#N#>Gamma-Ray Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second as Reactive Damage.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Gamma-Ray</>: Similar to Starfire in damage output, Gamma-Ray tears a hole in the sky to allow powerful gamma-rays to strike the ground, dealing reactive tick damage to enemies in the area. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) forces a Gamma-Ray to strike the ground in front of you, dealing tick damage to anything nearby until it goes away. The damage is dealt in a vertical cylinder in the location of the Gamma-Ray.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Gamma-Ray Duration: 10s<#N#>Gamma-Ray Radius: 1200 (4 Foundations)<#N#>Gamma-Ray Height: 6000 (20 Foundations)<#N#>Gamma-Ray Damage: 50% of Ability Damage Every 1/2 Second as Reactive Damage.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2144010215"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "214A81774A3C25CA272E31904FAB1EFB",
      "Source": "Comet",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Comet","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3900991518"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "177DB0DF4A894C1F63C05B8DC76117F3",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Comet</>: One large Comet. These creatures will create a single large comet that crashes into the ground in front of them. A direct hit means incredible damage is dealt, while an indirect impact will cause damage based on proximity to the Comet. Comet can make excellent Boss fighters with their high direct-hit impact.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) calls down a single Comet, which can deal great impact damage if it does a direct hit, with lesser damage for indirect hits.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Comet Impact Damage: 1000% of Ability Damage<#N#>Comet Impact Radius: 600 (2 foundations)<#N#>AoE Impact Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>AoE Impact Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 1, 1\">Comet</>: One large Comet. These creatures will create a single large comet that crashes into the ground in front of them. A direct hit means incredible damage is dealt, while an indirect impact will cause damage based on proximity to the Comet. Comet can make excellent Boss fighters with their high direct-hit impact.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) calls down a single Comet, which can deal great impact damage if it does a direct hit, with lesser damage for indirect hits.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Comet Impact Damage: 1000% of Ability Damage<#N#>Comet Impact Radius: 600 (2 foundations)<#N#>AoE Impact Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>AoE Impact Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2784905313"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "C15C6D4D4145946C17E55FAC333117A4",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">ELEMENTAL:</><#RN#>Elemental creatures are the most common creatures in Ark Omega. They have the power of any of 6 elements: Fire, Earth, Water, Ice, Wind, Lightning. They are also split into 2 types, Elementals and Storm Elementals. Each Element has a weakness to another, and a resistance to another. This works in a circular pattern, with every Element having 1 weakness and 1 resistance. Elemental creatures launch projectiles at enemies based around their element, causing impact damage, AoE explosion damage, and often a ticking damage that causes various status effects. Storm Elementals summon a swirling storm of their element around them, doing more damage in a much greater area, making them exponentially more dangerous.<#RN#><#RN#><RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">STANDARD ELEMENTALS:</><#RN#>Standard elemental variants launch projectiles based around their element. They also all get a crosshair when mounted to help aim them. These projectiles can travel a great distance, do AoE damage on impact, and cause status effects. They are also able to use this ability in turret mode, should that dino have access to it. <#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will launch an elemental ball from the head of the creature in the direction of the crosshair. The ones effected by gravity drop will fire at a slight angle upwards of 2 degrees so that creatures lower to the ground won't have their projectile immediately explode.<#RN#><#RN#><RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">BURST ELEMENTALS:</><#RN#>Storm Elementals are an enhanced version of standard elementals. They are more powerful, harder to tame, with more dangerous abilities and a greatly increased likelihood of inflicting status effects. Storm elementals creating swirling storms around themselves that damage and debuff anything trapped with them, making their AoE capabilities far beyond that of normal Elementals. Once you've established yourself a few standard elemental tames for egg production, and have gathered up a few good tranqs, it is highly recommended to step into Storm Elemental as battle mounts.<#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a swirling storm around the creature. These storms hit enemies in a nearby AoE, piling on status effects. Because of this, they can be extremely good for close range combat.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">ELEMENTAL:</><#RN#>Elemental creatures are the most common creatures in Ark Omega. They have the power of any of 6 elements: Fire, Earth, Water, Ice, Wind, Lightning. They are also split into 2 types, Elementals and Storm Elementals. Each Element has a weakness to another, and a resistance to another. This works in a circular pattern, with every Element having 1 weakness and 1 resistance. Elemental creatures launch projectiles at enemies based around their element, causing impact damage, AoE explosion damage, and often a ticking damage that causes various status effects. Storm Elementals summon a swirling storm of their element around them, doing more damage in a much greater area, making them exponentially more dangerous.<#RN#><#RN#><RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">STANDARD ELEMENTALS:</><#RN#>Standard elemental variants launch projectiles based around their element. They also all get a crosshair when mounted to help aim them. These projectiles can travel a great distance, do AoE damage on impact, and cause status effects. They are also able to use this ability in turret mode, should that dino have access to it. <#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will launch an elemental ball from the head of the creature in the direction of the crosshair. The ones effected by gravity drop will fire at a slight angle upwards of 2 degrees so that creatures lower to the ground won't have their projectile immediately explode.<#RN#><#RN#><RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">BURST ELEMENTALS:</><#RN#>Storm Elementals are an enhanced version of standard elementals. They are more powerful, harder to tame, with more dangerous abilities and a greatly increased likelihood of inflicting status effects. Storm elementals creating swirling storms around themselves that damage and debuff anything trapped with them, making their AoE capabilities far beyond that of normal Elementals. Once you've established yourself a few standard elemental tames for egg production, and have gathered up a few good tranqs, it is highly recommended to step into Storm Elemental as battle mounts.<#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a swirling storm around the creature. These storms hit enemies in a nearby AoE, piling on status effects. Because of this, they can be extremely good for close range combat.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2063267836"}
    },
