    {
      "NamespaceHash": "79C13089470ABE2A5C2C3183E3DDFE26",
      "Source": "Barrage",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Barrage","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2409668161"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E8E0EA1941B54B72905D2AAD05F308C0",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">Barrage</>: The 7th Variant of Elemental. Barrage rains down a rapid attack of chromatic cannonballs that impact as a random elemental ball. Many of them are fired in a short period of time, and they are fired directly at surrounding targets. There isn't any way to control which element they will deal damage for, but the damage dealt is usually formidable. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will start the Barrage, firing chromatic cannonballs directly at nearby targets.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Target Seeking Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Barrage Duration: 2.5s<#N#>Projectile Firing Cooldown: 0.25s<#N#>Barrage Impact Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Barrage Effect: Damage and Effect based on type of elemental impact.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 1, 0, 1\">Barrage</>: The 7th Variant of Elemental. Barrage rains down a rapid attack of chromatic cannonballs that impact as a random elemental ball. Many of them are fired in a short period of time, and they are fired directly at surrounding targets. There isn't any way to control which element they will deal damage for, but the damage dealt is usually formidable. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will start the Barrage, firing chromatic cannonballs directly at nearby targets.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Target Seeking Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Barrage Duration: 2.5s<#N#>Projectile Firing Cooldown: 0.25s<#N#>Barrage Impact Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Barrage Effect: Damage and Effect based on type of elemental impact.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2998001828"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "1FC21AE14927D811BF9AE290E4DB74A7",
      "Source": "ETHEREAL:<#RN#>Ethereal creatures are meant for travel and stealth. Not typically used for combat mounts, although they each have features that make them extremely useful.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"ETHEREAL:<#RN#>Ethereal creatures are meant for travel and stealth. Not typically used for combat mounts, although they each have features that make them extremely useful.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1288981710"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "830BC1474DBFBC782A820498953FE343",
      "Source": "Teleporter",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Teleporter","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2087059861"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0448B89B4EC7A5AA0FE8449E382BBDEA",
      "Source": "Teleporter: Teleporter creatures are able to travel short distances in a flash. They will teleport when hit unless ridden, to a random location in front of them. This will do explosive AoE damage at both the location it teleported away from, and the location it teleported to.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will instantly teleport. Holding Prone(X) will show the location indicator on where you are going to teleport to, and releasing will teleport you there.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Stamina Cost to teleport: 5%<#N#>Cooldown: 1s<#N#>AoE damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#N#>AoE radius: 600 (2 foundations)<#N#>Chance to Teleport when hit: 33%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Teleporter: Teleporter creatures are able to travel short distances in a flash. They will teleport when hit unless ridden, to a random location in front of them. This will do explosive AoE damage at both the location it teleported away from, and the location it teleported to.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will instantly teleport. Holding Prone(X) will show the location indicator on where you are going to teleport to, and releasing will teleport you there.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Stamina Cost to teleport: 5%<#N#>Cooldown: 1s<#N#>AoE damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#N#>AoE radius: 600 (2 foundations)<#N#>Chance to Teleport when hit: 33%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"884296559"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2F7195B643D91F1300323F87F19F81A4",
      "Source": "Spectral",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Spectral","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3869636452"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "33FE8A7E474679D4004E50BBA329CF87",
      "Source": "Spectral: These have the ability to go invisible on command, preventing wild creatures from seeing them. This ability has no cooldown, but instead drains stamina over time. Hitting zero stamina will cause them to uncloak. An additional perk of Spectral creatures is that they have a chance to dodge damage entirely while invisible, and allow riders to use weapons while mounted. Hitting a wild Spectral will cause it to flee, only to return when it uncloaks.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause them to instantly cloak, and pressing it again will uncloak. There is no cooldown on this ability.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Can toggle cloaking on/off with no cooldown.<#N#>Change to Dodge while cloaked: (Tier x 5)%<#N#>Stamina drain per second to cloak: 1%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Spectral: These have the ability to go invisible on command, preventing wild creatures from seeing them. This ability has no cooldown, but instead drains stamina over time. Hitting zero stamina will cause them to uncloak. An additional perk of Spectral creatures is that they have a chance to dodge damage entirely while invisible, and allow riders to use weapons while mounted. Hitting a wild Spectral will cause it to flee, only to return when it uncloaks.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause them to instantly cloak, and pressing it again will uncloak. There is no cooldown on this ability.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Can toggle cloaking on/off with no cooldown.<#N#>Change to Dodge while cloaked: (Tier x 5)%<#N#>Stamina drain per second to cloak: 1%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4115446619"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "DE4870AA41902C0F520ED2B9AA0EEB26",
      "Source": "Dimensional",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Dimensional","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2074925684"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "1155382E47B848A5F4C7C080CB230A80",
      "Source": "Dimensional: An ability you have to see to believe, Dimensional creatures completely ignore air and water. They have no concept of either. Dimensional land creatures can walk or fly right into the ocean, and Dimensional water creatures can swim right out into the sky allowing you to use your favorite water tame on land. The Jump(Space) can be used to toggle flight on even ground creatures. They use no oxygen, and with their Dimensional Vision activated, your rider will not use oxygen either.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will remove all water from sight, making it completely invisible. You will be able to see the very depths of the ocean floor from the sky, allowing unlimited underwater exploration. <#N#><#N#>NOTE: Dimensional water tames should not be left out during a restart. The game may see them as water tames before seeing them as dimensional, and delete them!<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Does not use Oxygen<#N#>Can travel in/out of water at will.<#N#>Can turn water to air, hiding the ocean completely from sight.<#N#>Stamina drain per second in Dimensional Vision: 1%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Dimensional: An ability you have to see to believe, Dimensional creatures completely ignore air and water. They have no concept of either. Dimensional land creatures can walk or fly right into the ocean, and Dimensional water creatures can swim right out into the sky allowing you to use your favorite water tame on land. The Jump(Space) can be used to toggle flight on even ground creatures. They use no oxygen, and with their Dimensional Vision activated, your rider will not use oxygen either.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will remove all water from sight, making it completely invisible. You will be able to see the very depths of the ocean floor from the sky, allowing unlimited underwater exploration. <#N#><#N#>NOTE: Dimensional water tames should not be left out during a restart. The game may see them as water tames before seeing them as dimensional, and delete them!<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Does not use Oxygen<#N#>Can travel in/out of water at will.<#N#>Can turn water to air, hiding the ocean completely from sight.<#N#>Stamina drain per second in Dimensional Vision: 1%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3178647402"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "8D2178C94E8C504AB49EF4B9D3D239D3",
      "Source": "Spiritual",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Spiritual","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2856951039"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0B1C77AD4D2AF951AE6177ACC7066D15",
      "Source": "Spiritual: While spiritual doesn't have a special ability, it makes up for it in other ways. Spiritual creatures are much faster than other variants, can carry more weight, and do not use stamina for movement including sprinting. These are the go-to mount for ease of taming and the ability to travel anywhere quickly while holding almost any amount of weight.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Does not use stamina for movement.<#N#>Weight Bonus: 10x<#N#>Speed Bonus: 2x",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Spiritual: While spiritual doesn't have a special ability, it makes up for it in other ways. Spiritual creatures are much faster than other variants, can carry more weight, and do not use stamina for movement including sprinting. These are the go-to mount for ease of taming and the ability to travel anywhere quickly while holding almost any amount of weight.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Does not use stamina for movement.<#N#>Weight Bonus: 10x<#N#>Speed Bonus: 2x","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1336485727"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "5065906A4CD992B9EA440B8F7E68E99E",
      "Source": "Warp",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Warp","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4020661586"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "EB4A111E43D58DD5692464A91D3D7BAE",
      "Source": "Warp: Similar to the Shadowmane's teleport attack, the Warp ability will teleport you between nearby enemies dealing damage to them. You can quickly attack many targets in succession, sometimes travelling a great distance while doing so. Unfortunately, you have no control over which targets are chosen.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) gets the nearest valid target to the Warp creature, teleporting you to it to deal damage before choosing another nearby target to continue. If a separate valid target is not found, the Warp is over.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Number Of Targets: Tier + 3.<#N#>Damage: 200% Of Ability Damage.<#N#>Warp Damage is affected by buff damage changes.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Warp: Similar to the Shadowmane's teleport attack, the Warp ability will teleport you between nearby enemies dealing damage to them. You can quickly attack many targets in succession, sometimes travelling a great distance while doing so. Unfortunately, you have no control over which targets are chosen.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) gets the nearest valid target to the Warp creature, teleporting you to it to deal damage before choosing another nearby target to continue. If a separate valid target is not found, the Warp is over.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Number Of Targets: Tier + 3.<#N#>Damage: 200% Of Ability Damage.<#N#>Warp Damage is affected by buff damage changes.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"996269239"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "1129683B453E2531BFAA308FD068BCCC",
      "Source": "Astral",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Astral","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3401861931"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2378541A4A500553EB282D8D5335D738",
      "Source": "Astral: While Astral Projectile doesn't have much combat use, it has a ton of support usage. Astral creatures have the ability to leave their body, moving around in the Astral plane. Passing through enemies will debuff them in several ways, giving either you, or allies, an edge in combat.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will allow you to enter Astral form. You cannot attack, take, or deal damage. Passing through enemies will apply a debuff.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Debuffs applied: Weaken<#RN#>Weaken Decreases Melee Damage Dealt By 50%, And Increases Damage Taken By 50%.<#RN#>Weaken Duration: 10 Seconds",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Astral: While Astral Projectile doesn't have much combat use, it has a ton of support usage. Astral creatures have the ability to leave their body, moving around in the Astral plane. Passing through enemies will debuff them in several ways, giving either you, or allies, an edge in combat.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will allow you to enter Astral form. You cannot attack, take, or deal damage. Passing through enemies will apply a debuff.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Debuffs applied: Weaken<#RN#>Weaken Decreases Melee Damage Dealt By 50%, And Increases Damage Taken By 50%.<#RN#>Weaken Duration: 10 Seconds","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1439117393"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "4DFDF5AA4B16D26FE62A06B68A19005E",
      "Source": "Disruptor",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Disruptor","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3567052135"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9B7CD2FF442D298442B507AA985F91DA",
      "Source": "Disruptor: The 7th Variant of Ethereal. This variant's purpose is to stop enemies from using abilities, which can turn the tide of almost any battle. This will not prevent passive abilities like Knockback or Resource shards, but rather activated abilities. It is also immune to damage from Disrupted creatures, allowing it to survive retaliation. One major bonus of this variant is that it removes dodge chance from Lucky variant creatures. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied to enemies which prevents them from being disrupted for 30 seconds. This pairs very well with Element Sickness from the Element variant.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) releases a wave of Disruption, stopping enemies from using Activated abilities, and even removing elemental immunities from Gods. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Disruption Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations).<#N#>Disruption Duration: 15s<#N#>Disruption Cooldown Buff Duration: 30s<#N#>Disruption Removes Lucky Variant Dodge Chance.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Disruptor: The 7th Variant of Ethereal. This variant's purpose is to stop enemies from using abilities, which can turn the tide of almost any battle. This will not prevent passive abilities like Knockback or Resource shards, but rather activated abilities. It is also immune to damage from Disrupted creatures, allowing it to survive retaliation. One major bonus of this variant is that it removes dodge chance from Lucky variant creatures. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied to enemies which prevents them from being disrupted for 30 seconds. This pairs very well with Element Sickness from the Element variant.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) releases a wave of Disruption, stopping enemies from using Activated abilities, and even removing elemental immunities from Gods. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Disruption Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations).<#N#>Disruption Duration: 15s<#N#>Disruption Cooldown Buff Duration: 30s<#N#>Disruption Removes Lucky Variant Dodge Chance.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2956920914"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "28DEE7D44E59461993C68B8746AED054",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">GUARDIAN</>:<#RN#>Guardian creatures provide mostly defense based abilities. These can range from protecting allies, to punishing attackers. Guardian creatures are very strategy based, with many potential purposes.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">GUARDIAN</>:<#RN#>Guardian creatures provide mostly defense based abilities. These can range from protecting allies, to punishing attackers. Guardian creatures are very strategy based, with many potential purposes.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"65776315"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "1C6659A14D89A0F831F39CB09CA88596",
      "Source": "Shield",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Shield","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2004651470"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E2C47AB14709FAC187CB909208A87105",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Shield</>:  <#RN#><#RN#>Shield is a form of tanking, applying a buff to nearby allies that negates damage they take for a certain amount of hits. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone (X) buff all nearby allies with the \"shielded\" buff, which negates all damage taken for an amount of hits based on the tier of the caster. <#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Radius: 2400 (8 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Shield</>:  <#RN#><#RN#>Shield is a form of tanking, applying a buff to nearby allies that negates damage they take for a certain amount of hits. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone (X) buff all nearby allies with the \"shielded\" buff, which negates all damage taken for an amount of hits based on the tier of the caster. <#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Radius: 2400 (8 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1539805961"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "BACA505E42C0F157D9EBA3BA1D22043F",
      "Source": "Reflective",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Reflective","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1148594567"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "D4323E714C228636ECA4A9A0020882C2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Reflective</>: Reflective creatures are another form of punishment. While reflection is active, Reflective create will reflect 100% of damage taken directly back to the attacker. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will activate Reflection, surrounded you in a razor sharp shards and forcing the attacker to injure himself when dealing damage.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Duration: 30s<#RN#>Damage Reflected: 100% of Damage Taken.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Reflective</>: Reflective creatures are another form of punishment. While reflection is active, Reflective create will reflect 100% of damage taken directly back to the attacker. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will activate Reflection, surrounded you in a razor sharp shards and forcing the attacker to injure himself when dealing damage.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Duration: 30s<#RN#>Damage Reflected: 100% of Damage Taken.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4079355133"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2A01F0314F1572F2E0CD8CA0D6641974",
      "Source": "Controller",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Controller","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3291042201"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "49949A8043B1D4B10BA2A79B56CB3E6E",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Controller</>: Controllers are in charge of aggression levels of nearby enemies. They can use a taunt that forces enemies to attack them, while debuffing the enemy so that they are stunned when attacking the Controller. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will taunt enemies, forcing them to attack the Controller instead of other allies. They can even make most passive creatures attack them. Attacking the controller while taunted will stun the enemy.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Taunt Cooldown: 10s<#RN#>Taunt Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Taunt Radius: 4000 (13.33 foundations)<#RN#>Damage Reduction While Taunting: 75%<#RN#>Taunt Duration: Depends on enemies aggro settings.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Controller</>: Controllers are in charge of aggression levels of nearby enemies. They can use a taunt that forces enemies to attack them, while debuffing the enemy so that they are stunned when attacking the Controller. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will taunt enemies, forcing them to attack the Controller instead of other allies. They can even make most passive creatures attack them. Attacking the controller while taunted will stun the enemy.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Taunt Cooldown: 10s<#RN#>Taunt Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Taunt Radius: 4000 (13.33 foundations)<#RN#>Damage Reduction While Taunting: 75%<#RN#>Taunt Duration: Depends on enemies aggro settings.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4273077162"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "46DA25F54908B39BDAC1D4AB499CE1BB",
      "Source": "Absorbent",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Absorbent","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3897405130"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B6DBCB2643F26C81CEDC299EA47F73D3",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Absorbent</>: Absorbent creatures are the ultimate tanks. They have a large health bonus, and reduced damage to compensate. They protect all nearby allies within their absorbent bubble, where all damage done to any ally is redirected to the absorbent creature. Even players within the bubble can dismount from their tame and join the fight, completely immune to damage. These are amazing strategy creatures, as even weaker creatures with high damage can join into Boss fights without worry of death. Stacking various potions and high quality saddle imbues on an Absorbent dino can make sure that nothing else takes any damage for the duration of a Boss fight.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will toggle the Absorbent Bubble. It has no cooldown timer, but instead drains stamina over time, so stamina potions are highly recommended as the bubble will deactivate once stamina has been depleted. Any and all damage done to any allied creature within the bubble will be redirected to the Absorbent.<#N#><#N#>Note: Absorbent and Guardian creatures cannot be protected by other Absorbents or Guardians.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second: 3%<#N#>Protection Radius: 2100 (7 foundations)<#N#>Additional Health Multiplier: 7.5x (15x overall health multiplier)<#N#>Additional Damage Multiplier: 0.1x (20% of normal damage output)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Absorbent</>: Absorbent creatures are the ultimate tanks. They have a large health bonus, and reduced damage to compensate. They protect all nearby allies within their absorbent bubble, where all damage done to any ally is redirected to the absorbent creature. Even players within the bubble can dismount from their tame and join the fight, completely immune to damage. These are amazing strategy creatures, as even weaker creatures with high damage can join into Boss fights without worry of death. Stacking various potions and high quality saddle imbues on an Absorbent dino can make sure that nothing else takes any damage for the duration of a Boss fight.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will toggle the Absorbent Bubble. It has no cooldown timer, but instead drains stamina over time, so stamina potions are highly recommended as the bubble will deactivate once stamina has been depleted. Any and all damage done to any allied creature within the bubble will be redirected to the Absorbent.<#N#><#N#>Note: Absorbent and Guardian creatures cannot be protected by other Absorbents or Guardians.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second: 3%<#N#>Protection Radius: 2100 (7 foundations)<#N#>Additional Health Multiplier: 7.5x (15x overall health multiplier)<#N#>Additional Damage Multiplier: 0.1x (20% of normal damage output)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"196865793"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "7C382BDC4D16EE8BC10F70A4F3B7EAFC",
      "Source": "Collective",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Collective","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1161076538"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "05F40DC7431FF0876F0384A0BCC19182",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Collective</>: Collective creatures serve many purposes. The main one being to punish damage dealers with their own damage. A collective dino is capable of going temporarily immortal, gathering and biding all damage taken over a short period, before exploding it back out evenly amongst all nearby enemies. Even weaker collective creature are temporarily immortal to Bosses, making them cheap expendable ways of punishing high damage creatures.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will activate the Collective ability, making the creature immune to all incoming damage for a period. The damage will add over the duration, and on deactivation will be exploded back outwards, divided up evenly amongst enemies. If there is only 1 enemy, it will take the full collected damage. If there are 10, they will each take 10% of the collected damage.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Duration: 15s<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 foundations)<#N#>Collecting Above Max Health Triggers Explosion.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Collective</>: Collective creatures serve many purposes. The main one being to punish damage dealers with their own damage. A collective dino is capable of going temporarily immortal, gathering and biding all damage taken over a short period, before exploding it back out evenly amongst all nearby enemies. Even weaker collective creature are temporarily immortal to Bosses, making them cheap expendable ways of punishing high damage creatures.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will activate the Collective ability, making the creature immune to all incoming damage for a period. The damage will add over the duration, and on deactivation will be exploded back outwards, divided up evenly amongst enemies. If there is only 1 enemy, it will take the full collected damage. If there are 10, they will each take 10% of the collected damage.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Duration: 15s<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 foundations)<#N#>Collecting Above Max Health Triggers Explosion.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2337864395"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "D69F1CE647682B1A2794E68DBD33C086",
      "Source": "Resilient",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Resilient","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3332455506"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "4AF5CC7D426A008E73B59ABEE4E9D935",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Resilient</>: A simple defensive variant, Resilient creatures gain resistances to damage types when attacked. The more they are hit, the more the resistances grow. Being hit by a different damage type will slowly reduce the resistances to others.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Resilient</>: A simple defensive variant, Resilient creatures gain resistances to damage types when attacked. The more they are hit, the more the resistances grow. Being hit by a different damage type will slowly reduce the resistances to others.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2461886280"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "39055CCA438DAC39992208AED77D403F",
      "Source": "Armored",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Armored","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1478539172"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "20F8278A4E083E93A01605AB0881F91D",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Armored</>: The 7th Variant of Guardian. Armored creatures gain increased damage reduction as their health decreases, making them increasingly more difficult to deal with as the fight goes on. Your best strategy is to kill them in a single blow, or get them below 1% health which will deactivate their damage reduction. Melee and Ability damages are also decreased as the Armored creature's health decreases.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Incoming Damage = Damage * Health Percent.<#N#>Melee and Ability Damage = 3 * Health Percent.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.4, 0.4, 0.4, 1\">Armored</>: The 7th Variant of Guardian. Armored creatures gain increased damage reduction as their health decreases, making them increasingly more difficult to deal with as the fight goes on. Your best strategy is to kill them in a single blow, or get them below 1% health which will deactivate their damage reduction. Melee and Ability damages are also decreased as the Armored creature's health decreases.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Incoming Damage = Damage * Health Percent.<#N#>Melee and Ability Damage = 3 * Health Percent.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3985206923"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "FE74350C4158B22BBD2DE7B4748B47E3",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">LUCKY</>:<#RN#>Lucky creatures are here to provide you with things for finding and killing them. They are very rare, but each has its own benefit when killed. They are fast, hard to find, and hard to kill. Killing them can also anger the god of their specific Variant, giving it a chance to spawn at an Omega Beacon.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">LUCKY</>:<#RN#>Lucky creatures are here to provide you with things for finding and killing them. They are very rare, but each has its own benefit when killed. They are fast, hard to find, and hard to kill. Killing them can also anger the god of their specific Variant, giving it a chance to spawn at an Omega Beacon.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"623804127"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "F1DACC6D4D1072C5E19BA0A7CB93EE30",
      "Source": "Loot",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Loot","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3535214786"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "DA03F05E4A128446F24D6CBBDBA57EF0",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Loot</>: Loot creatures are very elusive, and made of solid gold. They are very fast, have huge damage resistance, and drop a cache of items when killed. They are the easest way to get higher quality Ark Omega gear.<#N#><#N#>Loot dinos can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#N#>Drops when killed, with the Quality/Tier based on the Tier of the Loot creature: Tool, Weapon, Armor, Saddle, Tranqs, Resources, Food, Kibble, Potion, Ark Omega Item, Ark Omega Disposable.<#N#>Does not provide loot when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Loot</>: Loot creatures are very elusive, and made of solid gold. They are very fast, have huge damage resistance, and drop a cache of items when killed. They are the easest way to get higher quality Ark Omega gear.<#N#><#N#>Loot dinos can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#N#>Drops when killed, with the Quality/Tier based on the Tier of the Loot creature: Tool, Weapon, Armor, Saddle, Tranqs, Resources, Food, Kibble, Potion, Ark Omega Item, Ark Omega Disposable.<#N#>Does not provide loot when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2355420822"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "32CB15C84C0393E1B4AAF1AC043F155C",
      "Source": "Soul",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Soul","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3266057205"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9C8A28CD4CDD78406D73BA9B832EBCC2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Soul</>: Soul creatures are made purely of souls. Being made of such means they are also extremely hard to hit, as your attacks have a great chance of passing right through them. When killed, they drop a massive cache of souls. The number of souls dropped it based on the number of kibble it would normally require to tame that creature, so taming speed will have an effect on the number of souls dropped. The type of soul dropped will be based on the spawn rarity of the variants in that group.<#N#><#N#>Soul creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Chance to Dodge: 90%<#N#>Number of souls dropped: Paragon Shard Value x Tier X 10.<#N#>Does not provide Souls when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Soul</>: Soul creatures are made purely of souls. Being made of such means they are also extremely hard to hit, as your attacks have a great chance of passing right through them. When killed, they drop a massive cache of souls. The number of souls dropped it based on the number of kibble it would normally require to tame that creature, so taming speed will have an effect on the number of souls dropped. The type of soul dropped will be based on the spawn rarity of the variants in that group.<#N#><#N#>Soul creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Chance to Dodge: 90%<#N#>Number of souls dropped: Paragon Shard Value x Tier X 10.<#N#>Does not provide Souls when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2681920591"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "F4E2039B44BFED98F51990BC6CCC2B41",
      "Source": "Essence",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Essence","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2778640902"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "7E19684041695534D6D83EB34E631B60",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Essence</>: Often called \"gummy\" because of their appearance, these creatures are made of 100% pure Essence. Being made of such a fluid substance also means they take considerably less damage. When killed, they reward a huge cache of Essence based on their Tier. The number of essences dropped it based on the number of kibble it would normally require to tame that creature, so taming speed will have an effect on the number of essences dropped. <#N#><#N#>Essence creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Dodge Chance: 90%<#N#>Number of essences dropped: Paragon Shard Value x Tier X 50.<#N#>Does not provide Essence when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Essence</>: Often called \"gummy\" because of their appearance, these creatures are made of 100% pure Essence. Being made of such a fluid substance also means they take considerably less damage. When killed, they reward a huge cache of Essence based on their Tier. The number of essences dropped it based on the number of kibble it would normally require to tame that creature, so taming speed will have an effect on the number of essences dropped. <#N#><#N#>Essence creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Dodge Chance: 90%<#N#>Number of essences dropped: Paragon Shard Value x Tier X 50.<#N#>Does not provide Essence when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"793353145"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0DDEADFE4DE768FAFA2BD6B653E36005",
      "Source": "Paragon",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Paragon","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3013740179"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9214443B46A9365A9F9385A96D9FED51",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Paragon</>: Paragon creatures are greatly prized for their souls. When a Paragon creature is killed, it drops a soul based on its species. Feeding this soul to a creature of the same species will reward it a Paragon level, giving a permanent 100% stat increase, up to a Paragon level of 10. These are displayed on your tames name in Roman Numerals, with 10 being [X]. Because of this incredible power, Paragon creatures always spawn at Paragon [X], and are much harder to kill.<#N#><#N#>Paragon creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#N#>Chance To Drop Paragon: 100%<#N#>Does not provide Paragons when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Paragon</>: Paragon creatures are greatly prized for their souls. When a Paragon creature is killed, it drops a soul based on its species. Feeding this soul to a creature of the same species will reward it a Paragon level, giving a permanent 100% stat increase, up to a Paragon level of 10. These are displayed on your tames name in Roman Numerals, with 10 being [X]. Because of this incredible power, Paragon creatures always spawn at Paragon [X], and are much harder to kill.<#N#><#N#>Paragon creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#N#>Chance To Drop Paragon: 100%<#N#>Does not provide Paragons when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2152669092"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "31931BD746543B4FF3F658B5BBEEBF72",
      "Source": "Miracle",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Miracle","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"716550625"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "6F5EED0C4B69D1558CAB2CB0B6D4BEE5",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Miracle</>: These very elusive variants have the ability to change server settings when killed, changing many aspects of gameplay for a limited amount of time. They are rare, often hard to see, with a high chance to dodge, and increased speed.<#N#><#N#>When a Miracle creature is killed, if a new miracle is created or an existing one boosted, there will be a server wide notification that a Miracle has been performed. The miracles can be found in their own tab on the Guide.<#N#><#N#>Miracle creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Dodge Chance: 90%<#N#>Does not create Miracles when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Miracle</>: These very elusive variants have the ability to change server settings when killed, changing many aspects of gameplay for a limited amount of time. They are rare, often hard to see, with a high chance to dodge, and increased speed.<#N#><#N#>When a Miracle creature is killed, if a new miracle is created or an existing one boosted, there will be a server wide notification that a Miracle has been performed. The miracles can be found in their own tab on the Guide.<#N#><#N#>Miracle creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Dodge Chance: 90%<#N#>Does not create Miracles when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2177282872"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E8EDA92B480AC1134C03439578A866E9",
      "Source": "Treasure",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Treasure","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2445804031"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "00121B5D44383AB21629B88627777D7F",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Treasure:</>: Guardians of the chests, keepers of dynamic items, these living artifacts wander around holding the secrets to the locations of many items. <#RN#><#RN#>Killing a Treasure variant will give anyone nearby during its death a Treasure Hunter buff, revealing the location of any loot chests they come within range of and making it so your ridden tame uses 100% of your equipped magic find. <#RN#><#RN#>Treasure creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#RN#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#RN#>Treasure Hunter Buff Duration: 300 Seconds.<#RN#>Does not provide Treasure Hunter Buff when tamed.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Treasure:</>: Guardians of the chests, keepers of dynamic items, these living artifacts wander around holding the secrets to the locations of many items. <#RN#><#RN#>Killing a Treasure variant will give anyone nearby during its death a Treasure Hunter buff, revealing the location of any loot chests they come within range of and making it so your ridden tame uses 100% of your equipped magic find. <#RN#><#RN#>Treasure creatures can only be tamed using Unique Kibble.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#RN#>Damage Reduction: 90%<#RN#>Treasure Hunter Buff Duration: 300 Seconds.<#RN#>Does not provide Treasure Hunter Buff when tamed.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4094755771"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "49DDF5024204F7391F9D00B93D5095D3",
      "Source": "Cursed",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Cursed","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"504764783"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "C168B35247D39B8971D9509D2A4996AB",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Cursed</>: The 7th Variant of Lucky. A bit of a contradiction, Cursed isn't exactly Lucky. Cursed creatures apply random debuffs to enemies both when attacking, and when being attacked, and have a combination of both dodge chance and damage reduction. When killed, they drop a number of pre-cursed items using the curses from the Cursed Idol.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Chance to Dodge: 50%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 50%<#N#>Chance To Apply Debuff When Hit: 50% (10% With a Rider).<#N#>Chance To Apply Debuff On Attack: 50% (10% With a Rider).<#N#>Debuffs: Earth Poison, On Fire, Drenched, Stun, Electrocuted, Freeze, Banshee Curse, Rare Flower Aggro, Psychosis Aggro, Gorgon Stone, Detonate, Astral Curse.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.8, 0, 1\">Cursed</>: The 7th Variant of Lucky. A bit of a contradiction, Cursed isn't exactly Lucky. Cursed creatures apply random debuffs to enemies both when attacking, and when being attacked, and have a combination of both dodge chance and damage reduction. When killed, they drop a number of pre-cursed items using the curses from the Cursed Idol.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Speed Bonus: 100%<#N#>Chance to Dodge: 50%<#N#>Damage Reduction: 50%<#N#>Chance To Apply Debuff When Hit: 50% (10% With a Rider).<#N#>Chance To Apply Debuff On Attack: 50% (10% With a Rider).<#N#>Debuffs: Earth Poison, On Fire, Drenched, Stun, Electrocuted, Freeze, Banshee Curse, Rare Flower Aggro, Psychosis Aggro, Gorgon Stone, Detonate, Astral Curse.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2656256505"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "01A0C038458380528FCB409D17AC4BC2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">MYTHICAL:</><#RN#>All Mythical creatures are based on classic monsters from various mythologies. They possess the powers of these monsters or creatures and can wield them to be extremely useful in combat, both as damage mounts or utility.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">MYTHICAL:</><#RN#>All Mythical creatures are based on classic monsters from various mythologies. They possess the powers of these monsters or creatures and can wield them to be extremely useful in combat, both as damage mounts or utility.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3932985305"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "297E62B4410242F9527FDB9F17447636",
      "Source": "Phoenix",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Phoenix","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1285064016"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2B4DFB1B43FCFF2A6EEAC6B2F8767B2A",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Phoenix</>: Following the mythology surrounding the Phoenix, when killed it will simply rise from the ashes to be born again. Phoenix creatures can rapidly restore their own health when injured. When killed, their corpse will set ablaze, damaging enemies in the area. If its corpse is not harvested within 10 seconds, the Phoenix will resurrect.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will rapidly restore a large portion of the Phoenix creatures health over time.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#RN#>Health Restored: 10% per second for 5 seconds (50% of max overall)<#RN#>Corpse Burn before Resurrection Duration: 10s<#RN#>Corpse Burn AoE Damage: 1% of enemies max health per second.<#RN#>Corpse Burn AoE Damage Radius: 1000 (3.33 foundations)<#RN#>Phoenix Variants do not lose a tier when sent to the Reliquary.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Phoenix</>: Following the mythology surrounding the Phoenix, when killed it will simply rise from the ashes to be born again. Phoenix creatures can rapidly restore their own health when injured. When killed, their corpse will set ablaze, damaging enemies in the area. If its corpse is not harvested within 10 seconds, the Phoenix will resurrect.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will rapidly restore a large portion of the Phoenix creatures health over time.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#RN#>Health Restored: 10% per second for 5 seconds (50% of max overall)<#RN#>Corpse Burn before Resurrection Duration: 10s<#RN#>Corpse Burn AoE Damage: 1% of enemies max health per second.<#RN#>Corpse Burn AoE Damage Radius: 1000 (3.33 foundations)<#RN#>Phoenix Variants do not lose a tier when sent to the Reliquary.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2418243507"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "C3F496F244646CA19F51B49797ADE99F",
      "Source": "Gorgon",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Gorgon","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"832611844"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "C2FC46D247DF1A8E658FA18903858F45",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Gorgon</>: Like Medusa, one quick gaze from these creatures will cause you to turn to stone. Stoned creatures will be completely incapable of movement for a short time. Also, while turned to stone, creatures will take triple damage from any Gorgon that attacks it. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will instantly turn any enemy to stone caught within range of the Gorgon.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 20s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Range: 2400 (8 foundations)<#RN#>Stone Duration: 7 seconds<#RN#>Post-Stoned buff only allows creatures to be turned to stone once every 30 seconds. <#RN#>Attack Damage Increase vs stoned creatures: 3x",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Gorgon</>: Like Medusa, one quick gaze from these creatures will cause you to turn to stone. Stoned creatures will be completely incapable of movement for a short time. Also, while turned to stone, creatures will take triple damage from any Gorgon that attacks it. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will instantly turn any enemy to stone caught within range of the Gorgon.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 20s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Range: 2400 (8 foundations)<#RN#>Stone Duration: 7 seconds<#RN#>Post-Stoned buff only allows creatures to be turned to stone once every 30 seconds. <#RN#>Attack Damage Increase vs stoned creatures: 3x","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3804628996"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "16DB532B4AC3A76444AB1495D4B89B0E",
      "Source": "Siren",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Siren","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"452685737"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "D30A29EA40B7ED4E87430195FE0CB5D9",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Siren</>: These possess the ability to lull enemies into a completely passive state, forcing them to wander towards the music they hear. Siren's are capable of making even the most powerful of Bosses go completely passive, wandering towards the Siren completely unaware of its own demise, ignoring all damage dealt to it in the meantime. If your tame is hit by a siren while you are mounted, you will lose control and be powerless to control your dino as it wanders towards the Siren.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will make the Siren play a sound, making all creatures in the area go completely passive and wander towards it. They will not react to damage during this time.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Duration: 10s<#N#>Post-Siren buff only allows creatures to be lured by a Siren once per minute.<#N#>Range: 2000 (6.67 foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Siren</>: These possess the ability to lull enemies into a completely passive state, forcing them to wander towards the music they hear. Siren's are capable of making even the most powerful of Bosses go completely passive, wandering towards the Siren completely unaware of its own demise, ignoring all damage dealt to it in the meantime. If your tame is hit by a siren while you are mounted, you will lose control and be powerless to control your dino as it wanders towards the Siren.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will make the Siren play a sound, making all creatures in the area go completely passive and wander towards it. They will not react to damage during this time.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Duration: 10s<#N#>Post-Siren buff only allows creatures to be lured by a Siren once per minute.<#N#>Range: 2000 (6.67 foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3555998022"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "8C52B72A47AF56A032F01188E9195FD9",
      "Source": "Colossus",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Colossus","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4291623830"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "CAEB5C8F4924C55CE5EB5BBE81D05BDF",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Colossus</>: Massive creatures, significantly larger than original. They have greatly increased attack range, with ones able to land on the ground also being able to perform a powerful stomp attack on anything in the area. The stomp will not effect flyers or water creatures in the area. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) with a Colossus dino currently on the ground will perform a powerful ground stomp, also damaging other creatures on the ground. Water creatures and creatures currently flying cannot use the stomp, but are not effected by it either.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Range: 2100 (7 foundations)<#RN#>Damage: 300% of Ability damage.<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 50%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 100%.<#RN#>Colossus size, weight, attack ranges increased by: 300%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Colossus</>: Massive creatures, significantly larger than original. They have greatly increased attack range, with ones able to land on the ground also being able to perform a powerful stomp attack on anything in the area. The stomp will not effect flyers or water creatures in the area. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) with a Colossus dino currently on the ground will perform a powerful ground stomp, also damaging other creatures on the ground. Water creatures and creatures currently flying cannot use the stomp, but are not effected by it either.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#RN#>Range: 2100 (7 foundations)<#RN#>Damage: 300% of Ability damage.<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 50%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 100%.<#RN#>Colossus size, weight, attack ranges increased by: 300%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"649493588"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "611EDC1545B475D480529A91ED8FA9A9",
      "Source": "Fairy",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Fairy","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1688114490"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B55A6AD3431FA95CAB230C94F1E9CD41",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Fairy</>: Natural healers. A fairy will make an invaluable ally in battle, as it will heal all nearby allies for a % of their max health over time. An AoE healer that uses nothing more than its own Stamina to heal.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause it to heal any nearby ally on your team for a % of their health per second. Pressing X again will toggle it off and trigger the cooldown. The Fairy cannot attack while healing.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second: 5% <#N#>Healing Amount: (0.5% x Tier) of Max Health Per Second<#N#>Healing Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Fairy</>: Natural healers. A fairy will make an invaluable ally in battle, as it will heal all nearby allies for a % of their max health over time. An AoE healer that uses nothing more than its own Stamina to heal.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause it to heal any nearby ally on your team for a % of their health per second. Pressing X again will toggle it off and trigger the cooldown. The Fairy cannot attack while healing.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second: 5% <#N#>Healing Amount: (0.5% x Tier) of Max Health Per Second<#N#>Healing Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2023002415"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "407FFC274251A037765824A70025DC5B",
      "Source": "Pygmy",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Pygmy","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3655725698"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "48BF9CB2428FE66D71CC3186DA6FDC07",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Pygmy</>: Tiny terrors. Pygmys are a miniature version of their species, but don't let that fool you. Many pygmys can be packed into a very small area, and all Pygmys gain a pack bonus will all others regardless of Species. Prepare your tiny army!<#N#><#N#>Pygmy creatures cannot be ridden!<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Melee Damage Increase = 1 * (1 + (0.2 x Number of Pygmys))<#N#>Damage Taken = (1 / (0.2 x Number of Pygmys))<#N#>Max Pygmy Bonus: 30<#N#>Pygmy Bonus Range: 1800 (6 Foundations)(",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Pygmy</>: Tiny terrors. Pygmys are a miniature version of their species, but don't let that fool you. Many pygmys can be packed into a very small area, and all Pygmys gain a pack bonus will all others regardless of Species. Prepare your tiny army!<#N#><#N#>Pygmy creatures cannot be ridden!<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Melee Damage Increase = 1 * (1 + (0.2 x Number of Pygmys))<#N#>Damage Taken = (1 / (0.2 x Number of Pygmys))<#N#>Max Pygmy Bonus: 30<#N#>Pygmy Bonus Range: 1800 (6 Foundations)(","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"947882259"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "D7F290C24CF25830E237E1B213378281",
      "Source": "Druid",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Druid","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3943656344"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "538E7D594D9F5C77E4E599A7283F1CD0",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Druid</>: The 7th Variant of Mythical. Druid creatures leverage the power of the forest titan to raise toxic trees and ensnaring vines. While the vines to not deal damage, they root anything on the ground, preventing it from moving. The summoned trees will find the nearest enemy and begin firing projectiles that deal damage, slow, and blind. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) spawns a Druid Grove in front of the Druid creature, creating a large area of vines and spawning a number of trees that fire projectiles directly as nearby enemies.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Druid Grove Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Druid Grove Duration: 10s<#N#>Rooted Debuff Duration: 12s<#N#>Number of Trees Spawned: 7<#N#>Duration of Trees Spawned: 10s<#N#>Tree Projectile Fire Rate: 1 per second.<#N#>Tree Projectile Damage: 100% of Ability Damage As Earth Damage.<#N#>Tree Projectile Impact Radius: 600 (2 Foundations).",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 1, 0, 1\">Druid</>: The 7th Variant of Mythical. Druid creatures leverage the power of the forest titan to raise toxic trees and ensnaring vines. While the vines to not deal damage, they root anything on the ground, preventing it from moving. The summoned trees will find the nearest enemy and begin firing projectiles that deal damage, slow, and blind. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) spawns a Druid Grove in front of the Druid creature, creating a large area of vines and spawning a number of trees that fire projectiles directly as nearby enemies.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Druid Grove Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Druid Grove Duration: 10s<#N#>Rooted Debuff Duration: 12s<#N#>Number of Trees Spawned: 7<#N#>Duration of Trees Spawned: 10s<#N#>Tree Projectile Fire Rate: 1 per second.<#N#>Tree Projectile Damage: 100% of Ability Damage As Earth Damage.<#N#>Tree Projectile Impact Radius: 600 (2 Foundations).","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"598024546"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "371D756543D46C0B0612F0830868D2C4",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">NATURE</>:<#RN#>Forces of Nature, literally. Nature creatures are the ultimate elemental creatures, dealing elemental damage with abilities that are based on natural disasters. They easily rival Cosmic in their ability to dish out widespread damage and destruction. Afterall, this is their home turf. Nature creatures are rare, but should always be approached with caution. Their abilities are able to devistate large area, and often cannot be avoided or dodge in any way. They also cause elemental status effects and follow the elemental weakness/resistance system, so prepare those imbues!",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">NATURE</>:<#RN#>Forces of Nature, literally. Nature creatures are the ultimate elemental creatures, dealing elemental damage with abilities that are based on natural disasters. They easily rival Cosmic in their ability to dish out widespread damage and destruction. Afterall, this is their home turf. Nature creatures are rare, but should always be approached with caution. Their abilities are able to devistate large area, and often cannot be avoided or dodge in any way. They also cause elemental status effects and follow the elemental weakness/resistance system, so prepare those imbues!","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3524539212"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "FA754AD94D37EE58CF615B909EBCFB40",
      "Source": "Plague",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Plague","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"636453642"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "546B660348D6663D96941A8A95F2DDCE",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Plague</>: Plague is an ability with a lot of potential. When a Plague creature uses this ability, it will release a gas cloud, infecting enemies with a debuff. The infected will take tick damage as earth damage over a time, and if they die while infected, will erupt into their own Plague. This can create immense chains of Plague spreading across the land, wiping out huge groups of tightly packed enemies in seconds. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will release a deadly Plague Cloud that travels outward. This will infect all nearby enemies and they will immediately start taking tick damage based on the attack of the Plague creature. If killed while infected, each enemy will release an additional Plague, starting the chain over. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Plague Radius: 1800 (6 Foundation)<#RN#>Plague Tick Damage: 100% of Ability Damage Every 1 Second as Plague Damage.<#RN#>Plague Duration: 5s<#RN#>Enemies Killed While Plagued Spread a New Plague",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Plague</>: Plague is an ability with a lot of potential. When a Plague creature uses this ability, it will release a gas cloud, infecting enemies with a debuff. The infected will take tick damage as earth damage over a time, and if they die while infected, will erupt into their own Plague. This can create immense chains of Plague spreading across the land, wiping out huge groups of tightly packed enemies in seconds. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will release a deadly Plague Cloud that travels outward. This will infect all nearby enemies and they will immediately start taking tick damage based on the attack of the Plague creature. If killed while infected, each enemy will release an additional Plague, starting the chain over. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Plague Radius: 1800 (6 Foundation)<#RN#>Plague Tick Damage: 100% of Ability Damage Every 1 Second as Plague Damage.<#RN#>Plague Duration: 5s<#RN#>Enemies Killed While Plagued Spread a New Plague","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2473466917"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E4B59D654BECDCF3C9468FB6FCC5662D",
      "Source": "Thunderstorm",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Thunderstorm","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"83915584"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "85EF15284C5DFF234623C7B9C404E8B2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Thunderstorm</>: The name Thunderstorm might be a bit misleading. There are definitely lightning strikes. When Thunderstorm is activated, a powerful lightning bolt will strike one nearby enemy every second, dealing high impact damage, and spreading a static discharge in the area that deals tick damage to everything caught in it. The ability doesn't need to be aimed, as the lightning strikes seek out their targets, hitting without fail. This can be an amazing ability to use while fleeing or kiting enemies, as the lightning damage also causes electrocution, temporarily pausing their movement. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a powerful thunderstorm that strikes a random enemy within the radius each second, dealing strike damage but also creating an AoE static field that does tick damage. Lightning strikes ground flyers. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30% <#N#>Thunderstorm Duration: 10s<#N#>Thunderstorm Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Lightning Strike Damage: 100% of Ability Damage<#N#>Lightning Strikes Per Second: 1<#N#>Static Field Radius: 600 (2 Foundations)<#N#>Static Field Duration: 3s<#N#>Static Field Tick Damage: 20% of Ability Damage every 1/2 second.<#N#>Lightning Strikes Ground Flyers",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Thunderstorm</>: The name Thunderstorm might be a bit misleading. There are definitely lightning strikes. When Thunderstorm is activated, a powerful lightning bolt will strike one nearby enemy every second, dealing high impact damage, and spreading a static discharge in the area that deals tick damage to everything caught in it. The ability doesn't need to be aimed, as the lightning strikes seek out their targets, hitting without fail. This can be an amazing ability to use while fleeing or kiting enemies, as the lightning damage also causes electrocution, temporarily pausing their movement. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a powerful thunderstorm that strikes a random enemy within the radius each second, dealing strike damage but also creating an AoE static field that does tick damage. Lightning strikes ground flyers. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30% <#N#>Thunderstorm Duration: 10s<#N#>Thunderstorm Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Lightning Strike Damage: 100% of Ability Damage<#N#>Lightning Strikes Per Second: 1<#N#>Static Field Radius: 600 (2 Foundations)<#N#>Static Field Duration: 3s<#N#>Static Field Tick Damage: 20% of Ability Damage every 1/2 second.<#N#>Lightning Strikes Ground Flyers","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4050099489"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "933E0FD24705F20E87548AB0F5D216BF",
      "Source": "Eruption",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Eruption","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1138064913"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "EF90422243F96F3581AD6A83BE49F67D",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Eruption</>: Containing the explosive pressure of a Volcano, Eruption creatures are capable of blowing their top, spewing out molten projectiles in every direction that deal heavy damage on impact and large-radius explosive damage. With some careful practice, its possible to hit enemies with multiple Eruption projectiles for bonus damage.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will send a number of large molten projectiles into the sky, raining them down in random directions and locations around the Eruption creature, causing explosions on impact and dealing fire damage to anything in the area.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Number of Projectiles: 15<#N#>Initial Targeting Radius: 2400 (8 foundations)<#N#>Projecitle Speed: 2500<#N#>Projectile AoE Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Projectile Damage: 1x Ability Damage<#N#>Projectile Tick: 25% of Ability Damage Per Tick as Fire Damage (On Fire) for 6 ticks.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Eruption</>: Containing the explosive pressure of a Volcano, Eruption creatures are capable of blowing their top, spewing out molten projectiles in every direction that deal heavy damage on impact and large-radius explosive damage. With some careful practice, its possible to hit enemies with multiple Eruption projectiles for bonus damage.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will send a number of large molten projectiles into the sky, raining them down in random directions and locations around the Eruption creature, causing explosions on impact and dealing fire damage to anything in the area.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#N#>Number of Projectiles: 15<#N#>Initial Targeting Radius: 2400 (8 foundations)<#N#>Projecitle Speed: 2500<#N#>Projectile AoE Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Projectile Damage: 1x Ability Damage<#N#>Projectile Tick: 25% of Ability Damage Per Tick as Fire Damage (On Fire) for 6 ticks.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3496830213"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "6A9BE3EB4A87CD1D444135A0A9BA2B29",
      "Source": "Tornado",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Tornado","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1396975072"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "74788B5941A651B794F6F680E579FC3B",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Tornado</> A terrifying force of Nature, Tornado creatures can spawn a powerful twister in front of them, that can pick up, damage, and toss your enemies with great force.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a large Tornado in front of the Tornado Creature, that will pick up creatures and hold them for a short period, dealing Wind damage and stunning them. If an enemy dies inside of the Tornado, its corpse will be flung outward. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#RN#>Duration: 10s<#RN#>Damage Range: 3000 (10 Foundations) <#RN#>Damage Per Second: 100% Of Ability Damage as Wind Damage.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Tornado</> A terrifying force of Nature, Tornado creatures can spawn a powerful twister in front of them, that can pick up, damage, and toss your enemies with great force.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a large Tornado in front of the Tornado Creature, that will pick up creatures and hold them for a short period, dealing Wind damage and stunning them. If an enemy dies inside of the Tornado, its corpse will be flung outward. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#RN#>Duration: 10s<#RN#>Damage Range: 3000 (10 Foundations) <#RN#>Damage Per Second: 100% Of Ability Damage as Wind Damage.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1070948076"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "249674B747E9F6097E6C16B00BF79F16",
      "Source": "Tsunami",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Tsunami","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1279531608"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "578DD93D4CB8C78BD570F5BC5F9C92EA",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Tsunami</>: Tsunami creatures have the power to manipulate, even create, powerful waves of water that can damage, drown, and even push back enemies. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a poweful wave that quickly spreads outwards from the Tsunami creature. The wave will damage anything caught in it, drain their oxygen, and can even push them away from the Tsunami creature.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Tsunami Duration: 3.5s<#RN#>Radius: 3600 (12 Foundations)<#RN#>Damage: 600% of Ability Damage as Tsunami Damage",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Tsunami</>: Tsunami creatures have the power to manipulate, even create, powerful waves of water that can damage, drown, and even push back enemies. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a poweful wave that quickly spreads outwards from the Tsunami creature. The wave will damage anything caught in it, drain their oxygen, and can even push them away from the Tsunami creature.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Tsunami Duration: 3.5s<#RN#>Radius: 3600 (12 Foundations)<#RN#>Damage: 600% of Ability Damage as Tsunami Damage","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2705901802"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "363FD6774F66E42E494F9D9D3D936ACB",
      "Source": "Blizzard",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Blizzard","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3589563099"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "3D9D401640E871C7A2F13AA6C6DD950A",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Blizzard</>: Full control over Ice, Blizzard can be invaluable in combat. Activating Blizzard will summon a powerful cold-front that instantly freezes all enemies in the area, also dealing damage to them over time and freezing any new enemies that enter the Blizzard.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a freezing Blizzard, instantly freezing nearby enemies. Any enemies that enter the blizzard will slowly being to freeze. Everything will take damage over time while in the Blizzard.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Blizzard Duration: 10s<#RN#>Instant-Freeze Duration: 2s<#RN#>Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Damage Per Second: 100% of Ability Damage As Blizzard Damage.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Blizzard</>: Full control over Ice, Blizzard can be invaluable in combat. Activating Blizzard will summon a powerful cold-front that instantly freezes all enemies in the area, also dealing damage to them over time and freezing any new enemies that enter the Blizzard.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) creates a freezing Blizzard, instantly freezing nearby enemies. Any enemies that enter the blizzard will slowly being to freeze. Everything will take damage over time while in the Blizzard.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Blizzard Duration: 10s<#RN#>Instant-Freeze Duration: 2s<#RN#>Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Damage Per Second: 100% of Ability Damage As Blizzard Damage.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3983739155"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "7E2E0BCE40D50B63C1F1C0972EA6B81E",
      "Source": "Earthquake",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Earthquake","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1461917112"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2C89AFFD466ADF717426C0A0FE2020BD",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Earthquake</>: The 7th Variant of Nature. Creating an Earthquake has a lot of effects, from a screenshaking quake that applies stun, to all 6 Nature damage types spewing from the fissures in the ground directly on all enemies caught in the Earthquake. While it has minimal effect on flying enemies, it can be very damaging to ground based tames.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) causes the ground to shake, stunning all enemies in the quake radius and creating a fissure at the base of each ground dino in the fissure, dealing a random Nature damage type.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Earthquake Duration: 10s<#N#>Earthquake Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Stun Duration: 2s, applied every 4 seconds.<#N#>Fissure Damage: 100% of Ability Damage dealt as a random Nature damage type.<#N#>No Limit to the number of fissures within range.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0.25, 0, 1\">Earthquake</>: The 7th Variant of Nature. Creating an Earthquake has a lot of effects, from a screenshaking quake that applies stun, to all 6 Nature damage types spewing from the fissures in the ground directly on all enemies caught in the Earthquake. While it has minimal effect on flying enemies, it can be very damaging to ground based tames.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) causes the ground to shake, stunning all enemies in the quake radius and creating a fissure at the base of each ground dino in the fissure, dealing a random Nature damage type.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Earthquake Duration: 10s<#N#>Earthquake Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Stun Duration: 2s, applied every 4 seconds.<#N#>Fissure Damage: 100% of Ability Damage dealt as a random Nature damage type.<#N#>No Limit to the number of fissures within range.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2160162529"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "706182E443831F3C1A4287BCB579F227",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">NIGHTMARE</>:<#RN#>Nightmare creatures are the things that go bump in the night. During the day, they often behave like typical creatures. During the night, their abilities are greatly enhanced. They are also highly aggressive at night, often hunting you from a distance whenever you are in the area. Most nightmare creatures also gain Nightvision, with the ability to see enemies from great distances, even though walls, foliage, and terrain.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">NIGHTMARE</>:<#RN#>Nightmare creatures are the things that go bump in the night. During the day, they often behave like typical creatures. During the night, their abilities are greatly enhanced. They are also highly aggressive at night, often hunting you from a distance whenever you are in the area. Most nightmare creatures also gain Nightvision, with the ability to see enemies from great distances, even though walls, foliage, and terrain.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3921956622"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "8ACC87084A508CDDEA19B5A03EC336F6",
      "Source": "Zombie",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Zombie","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2514861773"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "84DA1E6246E4D04F692F2788151510E2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Zombie</>: Classic horror creatures in the flesh. Zombies are infected creatures that will turn their enemies into zombie minions on a killing blow. Those minions are also capable of turning enemies into zombie minions on killing blow, allowing you to quickly gather up a horde of infected. This makes the Zombie extremely effective in crowded areas and caves. Zombies gain bonus movement speed and damage reduction at night.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>Revives enemies as Zombie minions on kill.<#RN#>Zombie minions retain half of the paragon levels.<#RN#>Regains 5% of maximum health on kill.<#RN#>Nighttime Damage Reduction: 50%<#RN#>Nighttime Speed Bonus: 50%<#RN#>Zombie Minion Duration: 25s",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Zombie</>: Classic horror creatures in the flesh. Zombies are infected creatures that will turn their enemies into zombie minions on a killing blow. Those minions are also capable of turning enemies into zombie minions on killing blow, allowing you to quickly gather up a horde of infected. This makes the Zombie extremely effective in crowded areas and caves. Zombies gain bonus movement speed and damage reduction at night.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>Revives enemies as Zombie minions on kill.<#RN#>Zombie minions retain half of the paragon levels.<#RN#>Regains 5% of maximum health on kill.<#RN#>Nighttime Damage Reduction: 50%<#RN#>Nighttime Speed Bonus: 50%<#RN#>Zombie Minion Duration: 25s","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2646857209"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9AC12B6C4BF1C055D576698D58278D0D",
      "Source": "Vampire",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Vampire","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3146124339"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "BD19A59B41F4D312113CA184644BF08F",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Vampire</>: The Vampire is a merciless creature that waits for night to start hunting prey. Vampires will actively hunt players and tames at night, and during the night time they also gain night vision and the ability to heal based on damage dealt. They also gain damage reduction at night. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>Nighttime Damage Reduction: 50%<#RN#>Wild Vampires Will Attack Any Player Within 1800 Radius (6 Foundations) At Night.<#RN#>Nighttime Life Steal: 25% of Damage Dealt.<#RN#>Vampires Cannot Life Steal in the Presence of Starfire or a Dropped Hades Torch",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Vampire</>: The Vampire is a merciless creature that waits for night to start hunting prey. Vampires will actively hunt players and tames at night, and during the night time they also gain night vision and the ability to heal based on damage dealt. They also gain damage reduction at night. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>Nighttime Damage Reduction: 50%<#RN#>Wild Vampires Will Attack Any Player Within 1800 Radius (6 Foundations) At Night.<#RN#>Nighttime Life Steal: 25% of Damage Dealt.<#RN#>Vampires Cannot Life Steal in the Presence of Starfire or a Dropped Hades Torch","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4152375564"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2F76488443F9C5EB6C8D9690BF16D3B7",
      "Source": "Ghost",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Ghost","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"226483457"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "FF5824C64383BC443FA521B7F44F18AD",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Ghost</>: Hidden at night, terrifying at night. Ghost creatures are completely invisible during the day. You can walk right through them without knowing they are there, and they are unable to attack or be ridden during the day. <#RN#><#RN#>At night, they are the most powerful of Nightmare creatures. No special abilities, but exponentially more powerful with both increased health and damage, and a Dodge chance which prevents them from being hit.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 66%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 200%.<#RN#>Takes 4x Damage and Deals 75% Less In The Day (Tamed).<#RN#>Daytime Damage Reduction: 100%<#RN#>Nighttime Dodge Chance: Tier x 5%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Ghost</>: Hidden at night, terrifying at night. Ghost creatures are completely invisible during the day. You can walk right through them without knowing they are there, and they are unable to attack or be ridden during the day. <#RN#><#RN#>At night, they are the most powerful of Nightmare creatures. No special abilities, but exponentially more powerful with both increased health and damage, and a Dodge chance which prevents them from being hit.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 66%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 200%.<#RN#>Takes 4x Damage and Deals 75% Less In The Day (Tamed).<#RN#>Daytime Damage Reduction: 100%<#RN#>Nighttime Dodge Chance: Tier x 5%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2396168241"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "3960002B42241D2D14A1E0ABD34D3AE9",
      "Source": "Boogeyman",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Boogeyman","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1882571822"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "865499F1481ACD639BC22B9C58062E90",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Boogeyman</>: Ruler of the night, the Boogeyman is an absolute force to be reckoned with. A fairly normal creature during the day, at night they become covered in a solid black cloak, unable to be targeted by other creatures. At night, they also gain huge damage reduction, night vision, and the ability to jump-scare enemies with a powerful roar.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will make the Boogeyman release a terrifying Roar. This will do huge damage to the enemies, as if scaring the life out of them. It will also force them to flee for an extended period.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Roar Damage: 300% of Ability Damage<#N#>Roar Radius: 2400 (8 Foundations)<#N#>Damage Reduction at Night: 75%<#N#>Boogeyman cannot be targeted by enemies at night.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Boogeyman</>: Ruler of the night, the Boogeyman is an absolute force to be reckoned with. A fairly normal creature during the day, at night they become covered in a solid black cloak, unable to be targeted by other creatures. At night, they also gain huge damage reduction, night vision, and the ability to jump-scare enemies with a powerful roar.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will make the Boogeyman release a terrifying Roar. This will do huge damage to the enemies, as if scaring the life out of them. It will also force them to flee for an extended period.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Roar Damage: 300% of Ability Damage<#N#>Roar Radius: 2400 (8 Foundations)<#N#>Damage Reduction at Night: 75%<#N#>Boogeyman cannot be targeted by enemies at night.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"446993235"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "BA8E9F114D734B7B45ADCBA21FC47760",
      "Source": "Stalker",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Stalker","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3994327081"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9EC54BD24B5474BDFCDF30B29FDE83C8",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Stalker</>: Not something you want to think about following you, the Stalker will often cloak itself while in pursuit. While cloaked, it will not be targeted by enemies, and will uncloak on attack, landing a powerful critical hit.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) toggle the Stalker's cloak, allowing it to go on a hunt. Being cloaked will drain stamina, uncloaking when it is gone. If the Stalker finds a target and attacks while cloaked, it will deal massive bonus critical hit damage, also triggering the cooldown before it can cloak again.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost for Critical Hit: 25%<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second while cloaked: 2%<#N#>Critical Hit Damage Bonus: 500 - 1500%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Stalker</>: Not something you want to think about following you, the Stalker will often cloak itself while in pursuit. While cloaked, it will not be targeted by enemies, and will uncloak on attack, landing a powerful critical hit.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) toggle the Stalker's cloak, allowing it to go on a hunt. Being cloaked will drain stamina, uncloaking when it is gone. If the Stalker finds a target and attacks while cloaked, it will deal massive bonus critical hit damage, also triggering the cooldown before it can cloak again.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost for Critical Hit: 25%<#N#>Stamina Drain Per Second while cloaked: 2%<#N#>Critical Hit Damage Bonus: 500 - 1500%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1045955113"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "FD738A0042991BFCB9663FB112CA63F0",
      "Source": "Banshee",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Banshee","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3451167986"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "C155B1DF4D0BF726057138B084A89F67",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Banshee</>: Banshee's release a powerful scream, cursing their enemies and dooming them to death. The Banshee Scream acts as a powerful debuff, increasing damage taken for all nearby enemies.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause the Banshee to scream. Nearby enemies are cursed for a short period and will take increased damage. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Debuff Duration: 15s<#N#>Enemy Damage Taken: 175%<#N#>Maximum Number of Stacks: 3",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Banshee</>: Banshee's release a powerful scream, cursing their enemies and dooming them to death. The Banshee Scream acts as a powerful debuff, increasing damage taken for all nearby enemies.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause the Banshee to scream. Nearby enemies are cursed for a short period and will take increased damage. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Nightmare Vision at Night Time.<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Debuff Duration: 15s<#N#>Enemy Damage Taken: 175%<#N#>Maximum Number of Stacks: 3","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"89830823"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9A21CFEC47A0B8969092C483B9D57CBB",
      "Source": "Demon",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Demon","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1394073490"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "A370099C499C76882C899F8011881458",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Demon</>: The 7th Variant of Nightmare. Demon's have the ability to possess enemies, taking control of them, causing damage to them, using them to attack other enemies or allies, and more. While possessing another enemy, the demon cannot be damaged, and its location marked by a black soul.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will possess the targeted enemy, taking control of it for a short duration. During this time, you can use it to attack other enemies, or just sit idle with it allowing your allies to attack it. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Debuff Duration: 15s<#N#>Enemy Damage Taken: 175%<#N#>Maximum Number of Stacks: 3",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0, 0, 0, 1\">Demon</>: The 7th Variant of Nightmare. Demon's have the ability to possess enemies, taking control of them, causing damage to them, using them to attack other enemies or allies, and more. While possessing another enemy, the demon cannot be damaged, and its location marked by a black soul.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will possess the targeted enemy, taking control of it for a short duration. During this time, you can use it to attack other enemies, or just sit idle with it allowing your allies to attack it. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Debuff Duration: 15s<#N#>Enemy Damage Taken: 175%<#N#>Maximum Number of Stacks: 3","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2654905309"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "271D7865471574596490FA94DFCDDF72",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">RAGE</>:<#RN#>Pure Rage. These creatures are all about damage output. They can cause stun, bleed, enrage enemies, rally allies, cause knockback, go on rampages, or just be absolute death machines. Without normal AoE abilities, they can often be easier to tame, but also make incredible combat mounts. Rage dinos can also be incredibly useful in Boss fights, with a good selection of buffs and debuffs for many purposes.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">RAGE</>:<#RN#>Pure Rage. These creatures are all about damage output. They can cause stun, bleed, enrage enemies, rally allies, cause knockback, go on rampages, or just be absolute death machines. Without normal AoE abilities, they can often be easier to tame, but also make incredible combat mounts. Rage dinos can also be incredibly useful in Boss fights, with a good selection of buffs and debuffs for many purposes.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2229651047"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "643B126747E7298C7B0239A2D6021669",
      "Source": "Knockback",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Knockback","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3637305066"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "660431494D6E331083AA24BF362059EA",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Knockback</>: Keeping enemies at range, that's the point of the Knockback creatures. They have a chance with every attack to deal a blow that sends the enemy flying a short distance, leaving it temporarily stunned before it is able to re-enter battle. With enough consecutive attacks, a Knockback creature can keep an enemy outside of attack range, pummelling it without ever letting it get close enough to fight back.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Knockback Hits Deal Triple Damage.<#N#>Chance to Knockback/Stun: 25%<#N#>Stun Length: 3s<#N#>Impulse Amount: 400000",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Knockback</>: Keeping enemies at range, that's the point of the Knockback creatures. They have a chance with every attack to deal a blow that sends the enemy flying a short distance, leaving it temporarily stunned before it is able to re-enter battle. With enough consecutive attacks, a Knockback creature can keep an enemy outside of attack range, pummelling it without ever letting it get close enough to fight back.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Knockback Hits Deal Triple Damage.<#N#>Chance to Knockback/Stun: 25%<#N#>Stun Length: 3s<#N#>Impulse Amount: 400000","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2929625685"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "240573F9488D79FB04E236A3B59DD262",
      "Source": "Psychosis",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Psychosis","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"262075277"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "5A72049C47D183A44678F8AFA63821A2",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Psychosis</>: A Psychosis creature has an ear-piercing screech that sounds all other nearby creatures into a state of Psychosis, forcing them to attack eachother without prejudice. A player's own mount will being attacking and ignoring the players control. This can also prove valuable against enemies, as it will force them to attack other nearby creatures, even their own minions.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) releases an ear-shattering screech that drives enemies insane. They will become hyper aggressive, attacking the closest thing to them.<#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Psycho Scream Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#RN#>Psycho Scream Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Psychosis Duration: 10s<#RN#>Psychosis Gives Bosses A 10% Change To Damage Themselves.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Psychosis</>: A Psychosis creature has an ear-piercing screech that sounds all other nearby creatures into a state of Psychosis, forcing them to attack eachother without prejudice. A player's own mount will being attacking and ignoring the players control. This can also prove valuable against enemies, as it will force them to attack other nearby creatures, even their own minions.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) releases an ear-shattering screech that drives enemies insane. They will become hyper aggressive, attacking the closest thing to them.<#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 30%<#RN#>Psycho Scream Damage: 100% of Ability Damage.<#RN#>Psycho Scream Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Psychosis Duration: 10s<#RN#>Psychosis Gives Bosses A 10% Change To Damage Themselves.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1073467976"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2C5D579341B1BE42CE82B686BBB8BA61",
      "Source": "Uncontrollable",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Uncontrollable","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2390009654"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "68B2FC0841D96CFA708424BE7B68546E",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Uncontrollable</>: The most ruthless creatures in Ark Omega. Uncontrollables have very high stat multipliers that have no equal. They are highly aggressive, attacking any/all nearby enemies without fear for their own life. Wild uncontrollables will actively hunt players and tames. They are very fast, with a lot of health and damage. The name Uncontrollable comes from the fact that once tamed, they cannot be ridden, cannot be ordered or whistled, and will wander off to kill things while ignoring all of your commands. A powerful saddle on these creatures turns them into a death machine, able to easily take on Bosses with nothing more than the occasional healing dart to give them a boost. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cannot be Ridden<#RN#>Cannot be Ordered<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 75%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 300%.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Uncontrollable</>: The most ruthless creatures in Ark Omega. Uncontrollables have very high stat multipliers that have no equal. They are highly aggressive, attacking any/all nearby enemies without fear for their own life. Wild uncontrollables will actively hunt players and tames. They are very fast, with a lot of health and damage. The name Uncontrollable comes from the fact that once tamed, they cannot be ridden, cannot be ordered or whistled, and will wander off to kill things while ignoring all of your commands. A powerful saddle on these creatures turns them into a death machine, able to easily take on Bosses with nothing more than the occasional healing dart to give them a boost. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cannot be Ridden<#RN#>Cannot be Ordered<#RN#>All Incoming Damage Reduced By 75%.<#RN#>All Outgoing Melee Damage Is Increased By 300%.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"548481977"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "20A4C30B4EB8A6D1844F34A46D81D275",
      "Source": "Brutal",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Brutal","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3068718388"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0817D25543A9219475EDCAA4B6B98727",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Brutal</>: Brutal creatures have a chance on attack to inflict bleed, causing damage over time. The bleed damage inflicted is 50% of the damage dealt to the enemy, and will keep increasing by that amount up to a maximum of 3x the Brutal creature's Ability damage. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Brutal Chance to Stun/Bleed: 50%<#RN#>Bleed Duration: 6s since last bleed stack added.<#RN#>Bleed Damage Increased by 50% of Damage Dealt.<#RN#>Maximum Bleed Damage: 500% of Ability Damage.<#RN#>Bleed Damage Decay starts at 4 seconds and reduces by 25% of Abiilty Damage Every 0.5 Seconds.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Brutal</>: Brutal creatures have a chance on attack to inflict bleed, causing damage over time. The bleed damage inflicted is 50% of the damage dealt to the enemy, and will keep increasing by that amount up to a maximum of 3x the Brutal creature's Ability damage. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Brutal Chance to Stun/Bleed: 50%<#RN#>Bleed Duration: 6s since last bleed stack added.<#RN#>Bleed Damage Increased by 50% of Damage Dealt.<#RN#>Maximum Bleed Damage: 500% of Ability Damage.<#RN#>Bleed Damage Decay starts at 4 seconds and reduces by 25% of Abiilty Damage Every 0.5 Seconds.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3933154567"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B6F5118449F70A0F33A1749752115E89",
      "Source": "Rampage",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Rampage","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2399580662"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "D1C48BAA48934201C3C032A7CF433AE3",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Rampage</>: Rampage! These creatures have the ability to go on a Rampage dealing greatly increased damage. The more they attack, the more their damage output. Stop attacking for too long, and that bonus will start to decay away until they are back to normal damage and no longer in a Rampage. Nearby players will know that a dino has gone into a Rampage by the red glow on its head and the classic RAMPAGE video game sound that plays at this time. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will force the creature to go into Rampage mode. This will provide a Rampage meter, which increases with every attack, and decreases if time goes by without dealing damage. The % displayed is how much attack damage is increased.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60x<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Rampage Duration: 30s<#RN#>Maximum Rampage: 500%<#RN#>Maximum Damage Bonus: 300%<#RN#>Rampage Increase Per Attack: 10%<#RN#>Time before Rampage Decay: 3s<#RN#>Percent Rampage decrease per second: 0.5s",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Rampage</>: Rampage! These creatures have the ability to go on a Rampage dealing greatly increased damage. The more they attack, the more their damage output. Stop attacking for too long, and that bonus will start to decay away until they are back to normal damage and no longer in a Rampage. Nearby players will know that a dino has gone into a Rampage by the red glow on its head and the classic RAMPAGE video game sound that plays at this time. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will force the creature to go into Rampage mode. This will provide a Rampage meter, which increases with every attack, and decreases if time goes by without dealing damage. The % displayed is how much attack damage is increased.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60x<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Rampage Duration: 30s<#RN#>Maximum Rampage: 500%<#RN#>Maximum Damage Bonus: 300%<#RN#>Rampage Increase Per Attack: 10%<#RN#>Time before Rampage Decay: 3s<#RN#>Percent Rampage decrease per second: 0.5s","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"904908739"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "8B8D1F124686268D5011779E9BB3F377",
      "Source": "Frenzy",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Frenzy","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2582692536"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "08F787604BF4D8CEB8D2FAA16D604BB1",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Frenzy</>: Frenzy creatures make amazing allies. They have a powerful warcry that applies a temporary boost to nearby allied creatures, increasing their damage output. While it only lasts a short while, its enough to turn the battle when multiple creatures are used. This effect can also stack, meaning multiple warcries are enough to turn a small group into killing machines. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause the Frenzy creature to Warcry, increasing damage output for all allies in the area. Can Stack up to 3 times.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Warcry Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Warcry Duration: 15s<#N#>Warcry Damage Bonus: 75%<#N#>Maximum Warcry Stacks: 3",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Frenzy</>: Frenzy creatures make amazing allies. They have a powerful warcry that applies a temporary boost to nearby allied creatures, increasing their damage output. While it only lasts a short while, its enough to turn the battle when multiple creatures are used. This effect can also stack, meaning multiple warcries are enough to turn a small group into killing machines. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will cause the Frenzy creature to Warcry, increasing damage output for all allies in the area. Can Stack up to 3 times.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 25%<#N#>Warcry Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Warcry Duration: 15s<#N#>Warcry Damage Bonus: 75%<#N#>Maximum Warcry Stacks: 3","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4169937587"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "93F9DEA241F2A65C5668F9A2D6FD02DB",
      "Source": "Lethal",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Lethal","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1914748800"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E2EA984240CB3732F67EF99EB937698F",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Lethal</>: The 7th Variant of Rage. Lethal can help make quick work of even the most difficult Boss battles. When attacking with a Lethal creature, there is a percent chanced based on the damage dealt vs maximum health of the target to apply the Lethal Critical debuff. This buff triples damage taken from all sources, has a very long duration, and can stack up to 5x for a maximum damage multiplier of 243x. Each stack of the Lethal Critical Debuff also reduces the victim's melee damage by 30% (multiplicative) for a maximum reduction with 5 stacks of 83%.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Chance to Apply Lethal Critical Debuff: 1 / (Max Health / (Damage Taken * 3))<#RN#>Minimum Chance To Apply Lethal Critical Debuff: 0.4%<#RN#>Lethal Critical Taken Damage Multiplier: 3x Per Stack.<#RN#>Lethal Critical Maximum Stacks: 5<#RN#>Lethal Critical Debuff Duration: 300 seconds<#RN#>Lethal Critical Debuff Melee Reduction: 30%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0, 0, 1\">Lethal</>: The 7th Variant of Rage. Lethal can help make quick work of even the most difficult Boss battles. When attacking with a Lethal creature, there is a percent chanced based on the damage dealt vs maximum health of the target to apply the Lethal Critical debuff. This buff triples damage taken from all sources, has a very long duration, and can stack up to 5x for a maximum damage multiplier of 243x. Each stack of the Lethal Critical Debuff also reduces the victim's melee damage by 30% (multiplicative) for a maximum reduction with 5 stacks of 83%.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Chance to Apply Lethal Critical Debuff: 1 / (Max Health / (Damage Taken * 3))<#RN#>Minimum Chance To Apply Lethal Critical Debuff: 0.4%<#RN#>Lethal Critical Taken Damage Multiplier: 3x Per Stack.<#RN#>Lethal Critical Maximum Stacks: 5<#RN#>Lethal Critical Debuff Duration: 300 seconds<#RN#>Lethal Critical Debuff Melee Reduction: 30%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"750437495"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "A1D9919F462DA447E8A966AB2F766212",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">RESOURCE</>:<#RN#>Resource creatures are made out of their corresponding resource. They produce it, and poop it. They are much heavier than normal, and take 80% damage reduction. Their corpses are harvested as if you were harvesting a node of that resource. While they have no special abilities, they have huge passive damage reduction of 80% and when hit, have a chance to release a shard of itself, which will explode after a few seconds. Each resource type has an elemental weakness they bypasses their damage reduction. They also take double damage from the Multi-Tool, which can be used early on to kill and harvest these creatures, or KO them in club mode.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">RESOURCE</>:<#RN#>Resource creatures are made out of their corresponding resource. They produce it, and poop it. They are much heavier than normal, and take 80% damage reduction. Their corpses are harvested as if you were harvesting a node of that resource. While they have no special abilities, they have huge passive damage reduction of 80% and when hit, have a chance to release a shard of itself, which will explode after a few seconds. Each resource type has an elemental weakness they bypasses their damage reduction. They also take double damage from the Multi-Tool, which can be used early on to kill and harvest these creatures, or KO them in club mode.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"75221289"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "74A5B3D34793B5A04BBCD588CF05ED3B",
      "Source": "Metal",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Metal","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2241413042"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "836F3CE640384A485B0CC283FB57EF43",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">Metal</>: Made of metal, passively produce and poop metal. Taking damage may cause it to break off shards, dealing explosion damage in an area and applying a Splintered debuff that further increases damage from shards.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Elemental Weakness: Lightning<#N#>Harvested For: Metal<#N#>Drag weight increased: 3x<#N#>Amount of resource passively produced in inventory every 5 minutes: Tier x 10<#N#>Damage Reduction: 80% (20% damage taken)<#N#>Damage Taken by Elemental Weakness: 100%<#N#>Damage Taken by Multi-Tool: 200%<#N#>Shard Damage: 50% of Ability damage.<#N#>Shard Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Splintered Debuff increases damage from shards by 5%, and can stack 100x.<#N#>Shard Chance %: (Damage Taken/Max Health) * 2000<#N#>Shard Chance increases by 10% for each hit that does not produce a shard.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">Metal</>: Made of metal, passively produce and poop metal. Taking damage may cause it to break off shards, dealing explosion damage in an area and applying a Splintered debuff that further increases damage from shards.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Elemental Weakness: Lightning<#N#>Harvested For: Metal<#N#>Drag weight increased: 3x<#N#>Amount of resource passively produced in inventory every 5 minutes: Tier x 10<#N#>Damage Reduction: 80% (20% damage taken)<#N#>Damage Taken by Elemental Weakness: 100%<#N#>Damage Taken by Multi-Tool: 200%<#N#>Shard Damage: 50% of Ability damage.<#N#>Shard Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Splintered Debuff increases damage from shards by 5%, and can stack 100x.<#N#>Shard Chance %: (Damage Taken/Max Health) * 2000<#N#>Shard Chance increases by 10% for each hit that does not produce a shard.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2523156634"}
    },
