    {
      "NamespaceHash": "799AFC654DFDC23BFDA46FAC9D13114E",
      "Source": "Element",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Element","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"740617832"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "CFC10B834A19A8C83D4FD78A2EE918BA",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">Element</>: The 7th Variant of Resource. This variant's purpose is to stop enemies from using abilities, which can turn the tide of almost any battle. This will not prevent passive abilities like Knockback or Resource shards, but rather activated abilities, allowing it to survive retaliation. One major bonus of this variant is that it removes damage reduction from Lucky variant creatures. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied to enemies which prevents them from getting Element Sickness for 50 seconds. This pairs very well with Disruption from the Disruptor variant.<#N#><#N#>Element Shards apply the Element Sickness debuff, preventing enemies from using their abilities and removing Lucky variant's damage reduction. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied that prevents<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Element Sickness Duration: 5s<#N#>Element Sickness Cooldown Buff Duration: 10s<#N#>Element Sickness Removes Lucky Variant Damage Reduction.<#N#><#N#>Weakness: Explosive Damage<#N#>Harvested For: Element, Element Shards, Element Dust<#N#>Drag weight increased: 3x<#N#>Amount of resource passively produced in inventory every 5 minutes: Tier x 10<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90% (10% damage taken)<#N#>Damage Taken by Elemental Weakness: 100%<#N#>Damage Taken by Multi-Tool: 200%<#N#>Shard Damage: 50% of Ability damage.<#N#>Shard Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Splintered Debuff increases damage from shards by 5%, and can stack 100x.<#N#>Shard Chance %: (Damage Taken/Max Health) * 2000<#N#>Shard Chance increases by 10% for each hit that does not produce a shard.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 1\">Element</>: The 7th Variant of Resource. This variant's purpose is to stop enemies from using abilities, which can turn the tide of almost any battle. This will not prevent passive abilities like Knockback or Resource shards, but rather activated abilities, allowing it to survive retaliation. One major bonus of this variant is that it removes damage reduction from Lucky variant creatures. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied to enemies which prevents them from getting Element Sickness for 50 seconds. This pairs very well with Disruption from the Disruptor variant.<#N#><#N#>Element Shards apply the Element Sickness debuff, preventing enemies from using their abilities and removing Lucky variant's damage reduction. Upon deactivation, a cooldown buff is applied that prevents<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Element Sickness Duration: 5s<#N#>Element Sickness Cooldown Buff Duration: 10s<#N#>Element Sickness Removes Lucky Variant Damage Reduction.<#N#><#N#>Weakness: Explosive Damage<#N#>Harvested For: Element, Element Shards, Element Dust<#N#>Drag weight increased: 3x<#N#>Amount of resource passively produced in inventory every 5 minutes: Tier x 10<#N#>Damage Reduction: 90% (10% damage taken)<#N#>Damage Taken by Elemental Weakness: 100%<#N#>Damage Taken by Multi-Tool: 200%<#N#>Shard Damage: 50% of Ability damage.<#N#>Shard Explosion Radius: 900 (3 foundations)<#N#>Splintered Debuff increases damage from shards by 5%, and can stack 100x.<#N#>Shard Chance %: (Damage Taken/Max Health) * 2000<#N#>Shard Chance increases by 10% for each hit that does not produce a shard.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"476969150"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "074558E44D5FABC16994C6B4D422D166",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">SUMMONER</>: <#RN#>Summoners are able to bring minions into the battle to aid when its needed. Each of them has a very unique type of summon, and can be useful in a number of circumstances. The minions are not permanent, and will disappear after they're time is up. Minions cannot be ridden, or placed into a soul trap or cryopod.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">SUMMONER</>: <#RN#>Summoners are able to bring minions into the battle to aid when its needed. Each of them has a very unique type of summon, and can be useful in a number of circumstances. The minions are not permanent, and will disappear after they're time is up. Minions cannot be ridden, or placed into a soul trap or cryopod.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4158250673"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "4E95AC214CDE513986ECE9B333631760",
      "Source": "Necromancer",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Necromancer","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2532053818"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "04FA5E03431CB5DF0149BFAC887D395F",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Necromancer</>: Able to manipulate the dead, the Necromancer can revive nearby corpses to rejoin the fight, although on its side this time. As long as the corpses still exist, the Necromancer will bring them back to life, fully healed and ready for combat. They will retain almost everything they had in their life, including their abilities. The Necromancer can prove extremely valuable in many fights, bringing back the stronger fallen creatures to do battle for it, making it able to defeat things many times stronger than itself.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will revive all nearby corpses, restoring their tier and variant, allowing them to fight for the Necromancer for a short time. They are set to Attack My Target and Follow Me by default.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Corpse Revive Range: 2400 (8 Foundations)<#N#>Minion Duration: 60s",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Necromancer</>: Able to manipulate the dead, the Necromancer can revive nearby corpses to rejoin the fight, although on its side this time. As long as the corpses still exist, the Necromancer will bring them back to life, fully healed and ready for combat. They will retain almost everything they had in their life, including their abilities. The Necromancer can prove extremely valuable in many fights, bringing back the stronger fallen creatures to do battle for it, making it able to defeat things many times stronger than itself.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will revive all nearby corpses, restoring their tier and variant, allowing them to fight for the Necromancer for a short time. They are set to Attack My Target and Follow Me by default.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Corpse Revive Range: 2400 (8 Foundations)<#N#>Minion Duration: 60s","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1442485789"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "9458C4B445D0DD3B9428AE9C6EF8CCE6",
      "Source": "Overlord",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Overlord","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3648813626"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "97411A0E4A0F6AC22B8FC7AE4938F7E9",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Overlord</>: The Boss. Overlord's have dominion over any lesser creature of their species. When they call, a small horde of minions will appear of the same species as the Overlord, ready to fight for it to the death. These minions are smaller and slower, but the group of them is much stronger than the Overlord itself.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon minions at reduced size and speed. These minions will behave exactly as the Overlord, and are set to Attack My Target and Follow Me by default.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Minions: 5 Wild, 4 Tamed<#N#>Minion Size: 40%<#N#>Minion Duration: 20s",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Overlord</>: The Boss. Overlord's have dominion over any lesser creature of their species. When they call, a small horde of minions will appear of the same species as the Overlord, ready to fight for it to the death. These minions are smaller and slower, but the group of them is much stronger than the Overlord itself.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon minions at reduced size and speed. These minions will behave exactly as the Overlord, and are set to Attack My Target and Follow Me by default.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 45s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Minions: 5 Wild, 4 Tamed<#N#>Minion Size: 40%<#N#>Minion Duration: 20s","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1340279549"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "6BD3A9494182CAF88B7D19AE5E4FC3B3",
      "Source": "Cloner",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Cloner","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"247777064"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "DED1A70A41AB9AA2439FD9BBD3F83A62",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Cloner</>: Similar to Overlord, but against enemies, create multiple clones of your nearest enemy.If the enemy is much stronger than you are, it can clone that enemy, forcing to fight itself. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) clones the nearest enemy, forcing them to do battle with a copy of themselves. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Number of Clones created: 4<#RN#>Enemy scan radius (Enemy Clone): 2100 (7 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Cloner</>: Similar to Overlord, but against enemies, create multiple clones of your nearest enemy.If the enemy is much stronger than you are, it can clone that enemy, forcing to fight itself. <#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) clones the nearest enemy, forcing them to do battle with a copy of themselves. <#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#RN#>Number of Clones created: 4<#RN#>Enemy scan radius (Enemy Clone): 2100 (7 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"427399597"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "75978742444878E90125CFB903BE8255",
      "Source": "Random",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Random","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2604595566"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "AAFB97CC4B1E6FF47CF61C92E3ABD735",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Random</>: Random are the most unpredictable creatures in Ark Omega. They have no control over what they summon, as it can be any creature from any group. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon completely random minions, with random variants and duration. Even a Random Dodo can summon an Uncontrollable Titanosaur as a minion. Water dinos will only be summoned in the water. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Minions: 2-3<#N#>Duration of the Minion: 10-60 seconds.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Random</>: Random are the most unpredictable creatures in Ark Omega. They have no control over what they summon, as it can be any creature from any group. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon completely random minions, with random variants and duration. Even a Random Dodo can summon an Uncontrollable Titanosaur as a minion. Water dinos will only be summoned in the water. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Minions: 2-3<#N#>Duration of the Minion: 10-60 seconds.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1328321804"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2E1761AF44BD3A7322346C9EF6D7F8EC",
      "Source": "Companion",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Companion","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3957499444"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "7696C72D4E9910D59A21CCA537EE2ADC",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Companion</>: Everyone wants a companion. A minion that stays with you always, protecting you through thick and thin. The summoned Companion is very strong, takes little damage, and has a very special ability. It can steal the variants of anything it kills! You can only have 1 companion at a time.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a single Companion, which will stay with you until death, or you leave it. You can only have one companion at a time, so pressing X will destroy your current one and replace it with a new one. Your tame's melee and ability damage is added to that of the Companion's. Also, you can use the wheel to disable ability stealing when you get an acceptable variant.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#RN#>Cooldown for Variant Stealing: 10s<#RN#>Companion Base Health: 1100<#RN#>Companion Damage: 75 + Summoner's damage.<#RN#>Companion Damage Reduction: 50% against all sources.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Companion</>: Everyone wants a companion. A minion that stays with you always, protecting you through thick and thin. The summoned Companion is very strong, takes little damage, and has a very special ability. It can steal the variants of anything it kills! You can only have 1 companion at a time.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will create a single Companion, which will stay with you until death, or you leave it. You can only have one companion at a time, so pressing X will destroy your current one and replace it with a new one. Your tame's melee and ability damage is added to that of the Companion's. Also, you can use the wheel to disable ability stealing when you get an acceptable variant.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 60s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#RN#>Cooldown for Variant Stealing: 10s<#RN#>Companion Base Health: 1100<#RN#>Companion Damage: 75 + Summoner's damage.<#RN#>Companion Damage Reduction: 50% against all sources.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"653911095"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "490D00664AEAEC5F12877ABEA0702013",
      "Source": "Familiar",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Familiar","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3156672207"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "640466104EBBAD27D68F94B25A96B440",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Familiar</>: Many minions! The Familiar can summon a large group of angry bats, hell-bent on killing anything in the area. This swarm increases in numbers based on Tier, as does the individual strength of each bat.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon a group of Uncontrollable Onycs that will instantly begin attacking all enemies in the area for a short time. They will spawn at the same Tier as the Familiar creature.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Familiars: 5 + 1 Per Tier<#N#>Familiar Duration: 20s<#N#>Familiar Base Health: 250<#N#>Familiar Base Damage: 10% of its Summoner's damage.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Familiar</>: Many minions! The Familiar can summon a large group of angry bats, hell-bent on killing anything in the area. This swarm increases in numbers based on Tier, as does the individual strength of each bat.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will summon a group of Uncontrollable Onycs that will instantly begin attacking all enemies in the area for a short time. They will spawn at the same Tier as the Familiar creature.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 60s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40%<#N#>Number of Familiars: 5 + 1 Per Tier<#N#>Familiar Duration: 20s<#N#>Familiar Base Health: 250<#N#>Familiar Base Damage: 10% of its Summoner's damage.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3807654977"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "40FAB898425555E5E78BB093C4CF1B3C",
      "Source": "Overseer",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Overseer","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1485503374"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "1CC9836348321D75DA6F3CA55C009095",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Overseer</>: The 7th Variant of Summoner. Overseer summons a group of explosive bees, that swarm around their enemy waiting to die. These bees glow with the color of the summoner group before exploding and dealing aoe damage. If the bees are killed before they explode, then their explosions deal reduced damage.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) spawns a number of Martyr Bees, whos only purpose is to blow themselves up and deal area damage to whatever they lock onto.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Number of Martyr Bees: 7<#N#>Time Before Explosion: 5 Seconds.<#N#>Base Ability Damage: 12<#N#>Bonus Abiilty Damage: 10% of Summoner's Ability Damage.<#N#>Damage Dealt: 300% of Total Martyr Bee Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Damage Dealt if Killed: 50% of Total Martyr Bee Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Explosion Radius: 900 (3 Foundations).",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.25, 0, 0.5, 1\">Overseer</>: The 7th Variant of Summoner. Overseer summons a group of explosive bees, that swarm around their enemy waiting to die. These bees glow with the color of the summoner group before exploding and dealing aoe damage. If the bees are killed before they explode, then their explosions deal reduced damage.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) spawns a number of Martyr Bees, whos only purpose is to blow themselves up and deal area damage to whatever they lock onto.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Number of Martyr Bees: 7<#N#>Time Before Explosion: 5 Seconds.<#N#>Base Ability Damage: 12<#N#>Bonus Abiilty Damage: 10% of Summoner's Ability Damage.<#N#>Damage Dealt: 300% of Total Martyr Bee Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Damage Dealt if Killed: 50% of Total Martyr Bee Ability Damage as Explosive Damage.<#N#>Explosion Radius: 900 (3 Foundations).","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2679596177"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2F843897491FB128D5924A93E5C56093",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">UNSTABLE</>:<#RN#>Unstable creatures are as they sound, unstable. Without a moments notice, they could explode or erupt into powerful clouds and devistate would-be attackers. Unstable creatures can be unpredictible in fights, sometimes even riding the edge of death to deal the most damage. They are some of the more common massive AoE damage dealers you'll find.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">UNSTABLE</>:<#RN#>Unstable creatures are as they sound, unstable. Without a moments notice, they could explode or erupt into powerful clouds and devistate would-be attackers. Unstable creatures can be unpredictible in fights, sometimes even riding the edge of death to deal the most damage. They are some of the more common massive AoE damage dealers you'll find.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"4081700661"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "612ECC2A4B7151965DBB1CB24D664243",
      "Source": "Self-Destructive",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Self-Destructive","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2283461024"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B671D49B427BF6A70BEA28A386460343",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Self-Destructive</>: Self-Destructive creatures live to die. While they have no particular special abilities, they do explode on death, dealing damage based on their maximum health. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Self-Destruct Damage: 300% of Maximum Health<#N#>Self-Destruct Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Self-Destructive</>: Self-Destructive creatures live to die. While they have no particular special abilities, they do explode on death, dealing damage based on their maximum health. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Self-Destruct Damage: 300% of Maximum Health<#N#>Self-Destruct Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"236693395"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "36E2FCB64197409658431499E98DDF16",
      "Source": "Volatile",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Volatile","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1986862643"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "BF42A22E43894614F85F518560BEC5B3",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Volatile</>: These creatures are constantly on the edge of a bad reaction. They can spontaneously erupt into a powerful gas cloud, poisoning enemies and slowing them. This can happen both while they are attacking, or even while a passive Volatile creature is being attacked. This volatile cloud is dealt as Earth damage, so make sure your resistances are up before fighting the stronger ones. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) releases a small explosion followed by a volatile gas cloud. The cloud will linger for a bit, both poisoning and slowing enemies as it ticks away at their health.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40% <#N#>Initial Explosion Damage: 300% Ability Damage as Earth Damage<#N#>Initial Explosion Radius: 900 (3 Foundations)<#N#>Gas Cloud Tick Damage: 25% of Ability Damage Per Second as Earth Damage<#N#>Gas Cloud Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Gas Cloud Duration: 13 seconds",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Volatile</>: These creatures are constantly on the edge of a bad reaction. They can spontaneously erupt into a powerful gas cloud, poisoning enemies and slowing them. This can happen both while they are attacking, or even while a passive Volatile creature is being attacked. This volatile cloud is dealt as Earth damage, so make sure your resistances are up before fighting the stronger ones. <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) releases a small explosion followed by a volatile gas cloud. The cloud will linger for a bit, both poisoning and slowing enemies as it ticks away at their health.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 15s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 40% <#N#>Initial Explosion Damage: 300% Ability Damage as Earth Damage<#N#>Initial Explosion Radius: 900 (3 Foundations)<#N#>Gas Cloud Tick Damage: 25% of Ability Damage Per Second as Earth Damage<#N#>Gas Cloud Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Gas Cloud Duration: 13 seconds","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1948777839"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "44A8997D46D0DF4D365C63BD7E3C3724",
      "Source": "Explosive",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Explosive","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"276585112"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "778DE7CA46DD794467D6E79FC32BDCA4",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Explosive</>: As it sounds, these creatures can cause powerful explosions at any minute. Both while attacking or being attacked, these explosions may trigger doing damage over a large area as if a Grenade has gone off. Its best to avoid them unless prepared, as the explosion damage can destroy most structures as well.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will release an explosion, as if caused by C4 or a large grenade. The closer to the source, the higher the damage. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 10s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Explosion Damage: 300% of Ability Damage as Explosive Damage<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Explosive</>: As it sounds, these creatures can cause powerful explosions at any minute. Both while attacking or being attacked, these explosions may trigger doing damage over a large area as if a Grenade has gone off. Its best to avoid them unless prepared, as the explosion damage can destroy most structures as well.<#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) will release an explosion, as if caused by C4 or a large grenade. The closer to the source, the higher the damage. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 10s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>Explosion Damage: 300% of Ability Damage as Explosive Damage<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"208062164"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "0E408FB046FD79D933B96498E6F2DCF7",
      "Source": "Reactive",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Reactive","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"347638370"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "3C6BECF24C428C6A663B4C88B6C55E3F",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Reactive</>: Water is both the enemy and best friend of these creatures, as they have a violent interaction with it. When raining or entering water, the Reactive creature will start to emit a powerful aura of radiation and heat, doing passive damage to anything in the area. While a proven method for farming creatures, it can also draw unwanted aggro from enemies in the area that would otherwise not attack. Shortly after exiting the water, or the rain stops, the reaction will subside and the creature will go back to normal.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Reaction occurs when the Reactive creature gets wet.<#N#>Reactive AoE Damage: 100% of Attack Damage Per Second<#N#>Reactive AoE Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Reactive</>: Water is both the enemy and best friend of these creatures, as they have a violent interaction with it. When raining or entering water, the Reactive creature will start to emit a powerful aura of radiation and heat, doing passive damage to anything in the area. While a proven method for farming creatures, it can also draw unwanted aggro from enemies in the area that would otherwise not attack. Shortly after exiting the water, or the rain stops, the reaction will subside and the creature will go back to normal.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Reaction occurs when the Reactive creature gets wet.<#N#>Reactive AoE Damage: 100% of Attack Damage Per Second<#N#>Reactive AoE Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3272997737"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "5470EA644485B7D77AF8A99374026255",
      "Source": "Detonate",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Detonate","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1382924075"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "80E3A01B460630ADE1CFEFA5A269443B",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Detonate</>: Detonate is a very dangerous ability, if you're able to kill your targets. Detonate is a passive ability, which when hitting an enemy will debuff them for 5 seconds, indicated by a head on fire. If the enemy is killed while debuffed, it will explode, dealing damage to everything around it. There is also a chance that the debuffed enemy will explode when dealing damage to the Detonate creature.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Debuff Duration: 5s<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Explosion Damage: 100% of Detonate creature's Ability Damage<#N#>Chance for enemy to explode when dealing damage to Detonate Creature: 20%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Detonate</>: Detonate is a very dangerous ability, if you're able to kill your targets. Detonate is a passive ability, which when hitting an enemy will debuff them for 5 seconds, indicated by a head on fire. If the enemy is killed while debuffed, it will explode, dealing damage to everything around it. There is also a chance that the debuffed enemy will explode when dealing damage to the Detonate creature.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Debuff Duration: 5s<#N#>Explosion Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#N#>Explosion Damage: 100% of Detonate creature's Ability Damage<#N#>Chance for enemy to explode when dealing damage to Detonate Creature: 20%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"597086532"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "E6FA41484D0596F1F0ECDAA2A78429E9",
      "Source": "Meltdown",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Meltdown","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2071794907"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "323BFF3C4382169F65D1F3A15F7DB369",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Meltdown</>: A very high potential, yet very dangerous ability. Meltdown creatures can overheat themselves, sacrificing their own health, to deal stacking damage to enemies in the immediate area.<#N#><#N#>Holding Prone(X) will force you into Meltdown mode. You will lose health in Meltdown mode, and the rate at which health is lost will speed up the longer you are in Meltdown, but the damage also increases the longer you are in Meltdown.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Health Cost Per Second: 0.5% + 0.5% Per Second.<#N#>Damage Per Second: 50% of Ability Damage + 12.5% of Ability Damage Per Second.<#N#>Meltdown Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations).",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Meltdown</>: A very high potential, yet very dangerous ability. Meltdown creatures can overheat themselves, sacrificing their own health, to deal stacking damage to enemies in the immediate area.<#N#><#N#>Holding Prone(X) will force you into Meltdown mode. You will lose health in Meltdown mode, and the rate at which health is lost will speed up the longer you are in Meltdown, but the damage also increases the longer you are in Meltdown.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Health Cost Per Second: 0.5% + 0.5% Per Second.<#N#>Damage Per Second: 50% of Ability Damage + 12.5% of Ability Damage Per Second.<#N#>Meltdown Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations).","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"496527090"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "54444DC944021483EBF115ABCF6FD8DB",
      "Source": "Nuclear",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Nuclear","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3642123831"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B4EE097C4C32B6A7AF6D1B89565B0533",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Nuclear</>:The 7th Variant of Unstable. Similar to Meltdown, this allows you to sacrifice some of your own health to build up damage. But things here are a bit more interesting. Releasing the ability key, or reaching the limit, causes an explosion which deals a great deal of damage over a great area. This is the largest AoE attack in Ark Omega, and one of the highest damage multipliers, but use it carefully.<#N#><#N#>Holding Prone(X) will force you into Nuclear Meltdown mode. You will lose health in Nuclear Meltdown mode, and the rate at which health is lost will speed up the longer you are in Meltdown, but the damage also increases the longer you are in Meltdown.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Maximum Nuclear Meltdown Duration: 10s<#N#>Minimum Nuclear Meltdown Duration To Explode: 3s<#N#>Health Lost Per Second Of Nuclear Meltdown: 2.5%<#N#>Nuclear Explosion Damage Per Second of Meltdown: 300% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Maximum Nuclear Explosion Damage: 3000% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Nuclear Explosion Radius Per Second of Meltdown: 900 (3 Foundations).<#N#>maximum Nuclear Explosion Radius: 9000 (30 Foundations).",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"1, 0.5, 0, 1\">Nuclear</>:The 7th Variant of Unstable. Similar to Meltdown, this allows you to sacrifice some of your own health to build up damage. But things here are a bit more interesting. Releasing the ability key, or reaching the limit, causes an explosion which deals a great deal of damage over a great area. This is the largest AoE attack in Ark Omega, and one of the highest damage multipliers, but use it carefully.<#N#><#N#>Holding Prone(X) will force you into Nuclear Meltdown mode. You will lose health in Nuclear Meltdown mode, and the rate at which health is lost will speed up the longer you are in Meltdown, but the damage also increases the longer you are in Meltdown.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 30s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 50%<#N#>Maximum Nuclear Meltdown Duration: 10s<#N#>Minimum Nuclear Meltdown Duration To Explode: 3s<#N#>Health Lost Per Second Of Nuclear Meltdown: 2.5%<#N#>Nuclear Explosion Damage Per Second of Meltdown: 300% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Maximum Nuclear Explosion Damage: 3000% of Ability Damage.<#N#>Nuclear Explosion Radius Per Second of Meltdown: 900 (3 Foundations).<#N#>maximum Nuclear Explosion Radius: 9000 (30 Foundations).","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1135797912"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "429CDED54E85F84D0EF5CC911170421D",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">UTILITY</>:<#RN#>Utility dinos aren't meant for combat. They are here to serve a greater purpose. These purposes are usually centered around basic Ark functions, like taming or crafting. They can remove the need for increased INI settings for these basic Ark functions that often throw off balance and progression, by introducing a balanced way to reduce the need for grinding. Because of this, Utility dinos are often very rare, and their souls are used to craft incredibly valuable items.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">UTILITY</>:<#RN#>Utility dinos aren't meant for combat. They are here to serve a greater purpose. These purposes are usually centered around basic Ark functions, like taming or crafting. They can remove the need for increased INI settings for these basic Ark functions that often throw off balance and progression, by introducing a balanced way to reduce the need for grinding. Because of this, Utility dinos are often very rare, and their souls are used to craft incredibly valuable items.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3160432270"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "5A605E45403EE9DC47260FB1072D47BE",
      "Source": "Harvesting",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Harvesting","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3952291631"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "77E3060744CA68DA1240EF8C842E924D",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Harvesting</>: Harvesting creatures are able to harvest anything in sight. Even a Harvesting Rex can harvest stone, wood, and berries. They're meant to make gathering extremely quick and easy, reducing the need to boost harvesting rates (which would just obselete this variant). <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) does an area attack that harvests all nearby resources.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 5s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>AoE attack damage: 100%<#N#>Harvest Area: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Carnivores Harvest as a Hatchet<#N#>Herbivores Harvest as a Pick<#N#>Additional Weight Multiplier: 5x",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Harvesting</>: Harvesting creatures are able to harvest anything in sight. Even a Harvesting Rex can harvest stone, wood, and berries. They're meant to make gathering extremely quick and easy, reducing the need to boost harvesting rates (which would just obselete this variant). <#N#><#N#>Pressing Prone(X) does an area attack that harvests all nearby resources.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Cooldown: 5s<#N#>Stamina Cost: 10%<#N#>AoE attack damage: 100%<#N#>Harvest Area: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Carnivores Harvest as a Hatchet<#N#>Herbivores Harvest as a Pick<#N#>Additional Weight Multiplier: 5x","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3929565822"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "B0F3120644EF50D17CA7FEB52BB41FC5",
      "Source": "Taming",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Taming","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"1064566488"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "81BCEE7D4316DC50366C0DA5968EA906",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Taming</>: Taming dinos can make taming other creatures extremely easy. They all deal torpor! Taming dinos deal torpor with every attack, including some minor torpor over-time after the hit. This can be used to bypass the need for tranqs in some situations. Taming dinos also cause food to drain faster for KO dinos in the immediate area, increasing the rate at which they eat kibble and thus the speed at which they tame. NOTE: Taming dinos do NOT deal Raid Torpor. They will not KO any creature that requires Raid Torpor.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Torpor Multiplier: 500% of damage dealt.<#N#>Torpor Per Second: 500% of damage dealt over 5 seconds.<#N#>Food Drain Speed: Original Speed x Tier.<#N#>Food Drain Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Taming</>: Taming dinos can make taming other creatures extremely easy. They all deal torpor! Taming dinos deal torpor with every attack, including some minor torpor over-time after the hit. This can be used to bypass the need for tranqs in some situations. Taming dinos also cause food to drain faster for KO dinos in the immediate area, increasing the rate at which they eat kibble and thus the speed at which they tame. NOTE: Taming dinos do NOT deal Raid Torpor. They will not KO any creature that requires Raid Torpor.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Torpor Multiplier: 500% of damage dealt.<#N#>Torpor Per Second: 500% of damage dealt over 5 seconds.<#N#>Food Drain Speed: Original Speed x Tier.<#N#>Food Drain Radius: 1500 (5 Foundations)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3850414645"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "DB9FCB0143F281C4324F3AAB08731B60",
      "Source": "Crafting",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Crafting","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3383816616"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "14975A93476B4209DDE591B9BF0B577C",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Crafting</>: Crafting creatures provide a much needed service. They have a crafting tab in their inventory that contains nearly all engrams for everything in the Smithy, Fabricator, and Omega Workbench. They also get a huge boost to crafting speed based on their tier, meaning they can be used to bypass the Omega Workbench later in the game and craft all of your items at rapid speed. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Gains Crafting inventory of: Smithy, Fabricator, Omega Workbench, Kibble Machine, Replicator<#N#>Crafting Speed Bonus: (200 x Tier)%",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Crafting</>: Crafting creatures provide a much needed service. They have a crafting tab in their inventory that contains nearly all engrams for everything in the Smithy, Fabricator, and Omega Workbench. They also get a huge boost to crafting speed based on their tier, meaning they can be used to bypass the Omega Workbench later in the game and craft all of your items at rapid speed. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Gains Crafting inventory of: Smithy, Fabricator, Omega Workbench, Kibble Machine, Replicator<#N#>Crafting Speed Bonus: (200 x Tier)%","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"854199167"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "7F3C9ABB4A7FEDF2037BDDB7F0AAADF5",
      "Source": "Breeding",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Breeding","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"417470729"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "45CE03F8453F62450BE6219987B3D0B1",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Breeding</>: Breeding dinos alter various functions of Ark Breeding. They provide the Oviraptor Egg buff to nearby creatures, without the need to be placed on wander. This buff increases egg laying rates for any nearby creature with an egg icon above its head. <#N#><#N#>The main feature of Breeding creatures is their ability to greatly reduce the time needed between matings on nearby creatures. Feeding an unfertilized egg of the same tier or higher to a Breeding creature will activate a timer above its head to show how long the effect will last. Feeding multiple eggs increases the duration of the effect. This will cause nearby creatures that are currently in mating cooldown to have their timers tick faster, allowing them to mate sooner. This must be done by using the \"Consume All Eggs\" option at the bottom of the inventory screen or it will not apply the bonus.<#N#><#N#>PLEASE NOTE: The oviraptor egg buff does not stack with any other method of providing this buff. It is an Ark mechanic that modders do not have access to, and it cannot be made to stack. Placing a breeding dino with an Oviraptor, Hatchery, and anything else that provides this buff is a waste, as it will only be applied ONCE. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Provides Oviraptor Egg production buff<#N#>Egg Buff Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Buff Time Per Egg Fed: 5 Minutes<#N#>Timer Speed Multiplier: 1 + (Tier x 1)",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Breeding</>: Breeding dinos alter various functions of Ark Breeding. They provide the Oviraptor Egg buff to nearby creatures, without the need to be placed on wander. This buff increases egg laying rates for any nearby creature with an egg icon above its head. <#N#><#N#>The main feature of Breeding creatures is their ability to greatly reduce the time needed between matings on nearby creatures. Feeding an unfertilized egg of the same tier or higher to a Breeding creature will activate a timer above its head to show how long the effect will last. Feeding multiple eggs increases the duration of the effect. This will cause nearby creatures that are currently in mating cooldown to have their timers tick faster, allowing them to mate sooner. This must be done by using the \"Consume All Eggs\" option at the bottom of the inventory screen or it will not apply the bonus.<#N#><#N#>PLEASE NOTE: The oviraptor egg buff does not stack with any other method of providing this buff. It is an Ark mechanic that modders do not have access to, and it cannot be made to stack. Placing a breeding dino with an Oviraptor, Hatchery, and anything else that provides this buff is a waste, as it will only be applied ONCE. <#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Provides Oviraptor Egg production buff<#N#>Egg Buff Radius: 1800 (6 Foundations)<#N#>Buff Time Per Egg Fed: 5 Minutes<#N#>Timer Speed Multiplier: 1 + (Tier x 1)","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3225874668"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "2F33945C4B5A2FD1027FE6881FA38035",
      "Source": "Farmer",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Farmer","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3360003274"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "8E2EDD0E4C08C6645BDD39B29B7B88C8",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Farmer</>: Farmer dinos are invaluable to have in your base. They will passively pick up poop dropped nearby, convert it to fertilizer, auto-distribute to crops, and if they have an Unstable Water in their inventory, keep those crop plots watered forever. Once the crops have grown, the Farmer will collect the crops and berries from the crop plots and send them to your void vacuum to be distributed.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Poop Pickup Timer: 15s<#RN#>Poop Pickup Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Fertilizer Crafting Time: 900s/Tier<#RN#>Fertilize/Water Crop Plot Timer: 60s<#RN#>Fertilize/Water Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Will Provide Infinite Water With Unstable Water In Inventory",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Farmer</>: Farmer dinos are invaluable to have in your base. They will passively pick up poop dropped nearby, convert it to fertilizer, auto-distribute to crops, and if they have an Unstable Water in their inventory, keep those crop plots watered forever. Once the crops have grown, the Farmer will collect the crops and berries from the crop plots and send them to your void vacuum to be distributed.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Poop Pickup Timer: 15s<#RN#>Poop Pickup Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Fertilizer Crafting Time: 900s/Tier<#RN#>Fertilize/Water Crop Plot Timer: 60s<#RN#>Fertilize/Water Radius: 3000 (10 Foundations)<#RN#>Will Provide Infinite Water With Unstable Water In Inventory","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2990479748"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "6782AC954C0220AA4E74D9ABB256B25A",
      "Source": "Tracker",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Tracker","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3570032144"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "46728D83455B11EA35DF9CB8553F9B35",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Tracker</>: Trackers are one the rarest of all variants, and for good reason. A Tracker can find all Ark Omega creatures, displaying their location and using an indicator in their color of their Tier.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will send out a tracking signal, highlighting all nearby Ark Omega dinos by Tier.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 70%<#RN#>Tracking Base Radius: 15000 (50 Foundations)<#RN#>Tracking Radius Per Tier: 3900 (13 Foundations)<#RN#>Notification is provided when a Unique is found.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Tracker</>: Trackers are one the rarest of all variants, and for good reason. A Tracker can find all Ark Omega creatures, displaying their location and using an indicator in their color of their Tier.<#RN#><#RN#>Pressing Prone(X) will send out a tracking signal, highlighting all nearby Ark Omega dinos by Tier.<#RN#><#RN#>_____<#RN#>Cooldown: 30s<#RN#>Stamina Cost: 70%<#RN#>Tracking Base Radius: 15000 (50 Foundations)<#RN#>Tracking Radius Per Tier: 3900 (13 Foundations)<#RN#>Notification is provided when a Unique is found.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2672386657"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "A791246747A20FCF10ACE08D44C56DED",
      "Source": "Potion",
      "Trans": {"SC":"Potion","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"3312669876"}
    },
    {
      "NamespaceHash": "89A1551947760BF57524D4A204D3D478",
      "Source": "<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Potion</>: The 7th Variant of Utility. One of the most useful variants of all, Potion creatures are capable of feeding potions from their inventory to nearby players and tames to restore their health and stamina. The wheel can be used to set a health %, and anytime a nearby player or tame gets below that health %, they will have health potions and/or stamina potions fed to them. The maximum tier of potion that can be fed is limited to the tier of the Potion dino.<#N#><#N#>Only one potion type can be automatically fed at a time to your tames through a potion dino, so make sure to keep the highest tier health and stamina potions that it is capable of feeding.<#N#><#N#>Endless tier can feed Godlike potions.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Must put health/stamina potions into the Potion creature's inventory.<#N#>Only Basic through Omega potions can be used.<#N#>Health % to start feeding potions adjustable via wheel.",
      "Trans": {"SC":"<RichColor Color=\"0.2, 0.1, 0, 1\">Potion</>: The 7th Variant of Utility. One of the most useful variants of all, Potion creatures are capable of feeding potions from their inventory to nearby players and tames to restore their health and stamina. The wheel can be used to set a health %, and anytime a nearby player or tame gets below that health %, they will have health potions and/or stamina potions fed to them. The maximum tier of potion that can be fed is limited to the tier of the Potion dino.<#N#><#N#>Only one potion type can be automatically fed at a time to your tames through a potion dino, so make sure to keep the highest tier health and stamina potions that it is capable of feeding.<#N#><#N#>Endless tier can feed Godlike potions.<#N#><#N#>_____<#N#>Must put health/stamina potions into the Potion creature's inventory.<#N#>Only Basic through Omega potions can be used.<#N#>Health % to start feeding potions adjustable via wheel.","JA":""},
      "Config": {"Item":false,"Dino":false,"Default_Hash":"2180213582"}
    },
    {
